    #      styles::Color has, each view attribute one 18.3.1.87 names, or a
    #      namespace declaration), each with a control, and checks every tool
    #      line's sheetpr_before, tabcolor_before, views_before and kept_attrs
    #      against it.
    #  LE. specs/0024 P1 verification ruling 6 (P2's KD): every row ok; a
    #      refusal by the layer is still counted by row and message, and fails
    #      the summary.
    #  LF. specs/0024 P1 verification ruling 6 (P2's KE and KF): the entries
    #      table wants the flag descriptor on W's changed row exactly when the
    #      input's local header sets bit 3 and no flag elsewhere, the summary's
    #      flagged total checked against the sum the --parts lines give; the
    #      comparison checks the pair's xml values rows are W's alone, with
    #      in_only and out_only the one-sided counts of the values the design
    #      removes and writes, keyed by resolved element and attribute names as
    #      xlsx-diff keys them (xml_values), and the descriptor flags (flagged);
    #      the totals over the ok workbooks are printed and checked, out_only at
    #      least one.
    #  LG. NEW, specs/0024 P3 verification ruling 5 (carried by its close-out
    #      ruling 3) as specs/0025 "Harness runs" words it: the corpus runs take
    #      TMPDIR=<work>/tmp-run, made by this script on the disk; the device of
    #      it and of <corpus>/corpus are printed and checked equal, with a
    #      control (/proc's device differs); after each label's run the
    #      directory is checked empty (the runner's own temporary is removed by
    #      its own trap).
    #  LH. NEW, specs/0024 P2 verification ruling 6: every flag's planted control
    #      runs twice, on the first ok workbook in manifest order whose <sheetPr>
    #      is created and on the first whose <sheetPr> is kept, each on its own
    #      check line; a case the corpus does not hold fails its line.
    #  LI. specs/0024 "Planning rulings during P2" ruling 1, as P2's KI reads JI:
    #      this script runs no `rm -rf`; the sourced scripts/counting.sh, a
    #      committed script, runs one on the directory its counting controls make
    #      (allowed: a directory the script created in that run). JI's sentence
    #      "No `rm -rf` anywhere" above is that history; the working directory
    #      and the keeps stand, kept, and Python writes no bytecode.
    #
    #
    # CARRIED TO M3 part 3 P2 from M3 part 3 P1's run script (at the phase
    # commit 9db5f4f, printed in records/logs/m3p3-p1/run.log; its change list
    # LA to LI is above), generated by <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p3-p2/gen/
    # run.py, every replacement asserted to occur as often as it says, the top
    # summary and four blocks of the body replaced whole by their anchor lines,
    # and the body grepped afterwards for P1's names, subjects, stems and the
    # tokens svcmp, svsurvey, sheetview, m3p3-p1 and "M3 part 2 P3". What
    # differs, and why:
    #  MA. The phase, the log directory, the subjects, the script directory
    #      (<scripts>, <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p3-p2/scripts, on the disk),
    #      the build directory (m3p3-p2/run) and the keep (m3p3-p2/keep-host) are
    #      this phase's; the base is M3 part 3 P1's record commit ("M3 part 3 P1
    #      record:"); the phase commit is P2's tool commit by its subject; the
    #      record stems are m3p3-p2- and m3p3-open-; the spec's committed blob
    #      at P2's doc commit is pinned through SPEC_SHA, planning's rulings
    #      during P2 standing uncommitted in the working tree's copy.
    #  MB. Change LB's form, as M3 part 2 P2's KB read JB: the committed
    #      open-check record the keep is compared with is P1's, named by its
    #      record commit, resolved by its subject ("M3 part 3 P1 record:"; no
    #      hash is typed here), checked to be a record commit that added exactly
    #      one open-check .txt with no later commit adding another; it is this
    #      phase's base itself, the parent of P2's doc commit, which the check
    #      asserts in place of LB's "an ancestor of the base, not the base"; the
    #      control names P2's doc commit, whose subject is not a record's.
    #  MC. The comparison is pscmp.py, written for this phase on svcmp.py's
    #      readers; the checks are --pagesetup-sample's (specs/0025 "Harness
    #      runs", "The pass", rulings 1 to 3 during P2), its flags listed in its
    #      docstring, printed below; --parts as LC's. The line's relations are
    #      the spec's: each of printOptions, pageMargins, pageSetup and
    #      headerFooter 1 after, rid_kept, fit_ok, margin_ok, orient_ok,
    #      header_ok and footer_ok 1; the tool's counts equal the comparison's
    #      (the four before and after, the other headerFooter children, the
    #      relationships prefix). The entries: W changed, every other entry
    #      identical; nothing added, recompressed or dropped. The edit's shapes
    #      (which of the five and the pageSetUpPr are created) are printed per
    #      workbook and totalled. The comparison's xml values expectation is the
    #      one-sided count of the input W's values against the design's W's,
    #      keyed as xlsx-diff keys a value (LF's rule, derived from both sides
    #      whole rather than from the edited elements).
    #  MD. NEW, the survey (pssurvey.py, <scripts>, copied into <work> and
    #      printed) replaces LD's: it takes <corpus> as its parameter, lists
    #      <corpus>/corpus (every regular file, no extension glob; the count
    #      checked against the manifest's rows) and prints, for EVERY worksheet
    #      part of every workbook (ruling 3 of "Planning rulings during P2": the
    #      written order is the order the corpus's parts carry, read from this
    #      survey), the attribute names of the first <printOptions>,
    #      <pageMargins>, <pageSetup>, <headerFooter> and <sheetPr>'s
    #      <pageSetUpPr>, and the <headerFooter> child names; then for W the
    #      counts the tool's before-figures are checked against. The log prints
    #      each element's sequences with their counts, checks the forms (every
    #      attribute one the schema names for its element, or a namespace
    #      declaration, or a relationship id on <pageSetup>; the <headerFooter>
    #      children in 18.3.1.46's order; at most one of each of the four and of
    #      <sheetPr> on W), and checks that no surveyed sequence orders two of
    #      the attributes this part writes otherwise than the order the crate
    #      writes them in (ruling 3), each with a control.
    #  ME. Change LE (every row ok), LF (the descriptor flags and the derived
    #      values) and LG (TMPDIR on the disk for the corpus runs, its device
    #      against the corpus directory's) stand, unchanged.
    #  MF. NEW, specs/0025 P1 verification ruling 3 (L2): the open check's own
    #      TMPDIR, <work>/tmp, has its device printed beside the runs' and the
    #      corpus directory's and checked equal to the corpus directory's, with
    #      /proc's as the control, as LG's.
    #  MG. The plants: every flag's planted control runs on the first ok
    #      workbook in manifest order whose <printOptions> or <headerFooter> is
    #      created and on the first where both are kept, as LH's, each on its own
    #      check line; a case the corpus does not hold fails its line.
    #  MH. The run loop, the record pair, the keep and the open check are LC's
    #      to LH's with this phase's names; nothing else changes in them.
    #  MI. LI stands: this script runs no `rm -rf`; the sourced
    #      scripts/counting.sh, a committed script, runs one on the directory its
    #      counting controls make (allowed: a directory the script created in
    #      that run); the working directory and the keeps stand, kept, and
    #      Python writes no bytecode.
    #
    #
    # CARRIED TO M3 part 3 P3 from M3 part 3 P2's run script (at the phase
    # commit a6cf46f, printed in records/logs/m3p3-p2/run.log; its change lists
    # LA to LI and MA to MI are above), generated by <home>/.cache/emend-build/
    # m3p3-p3/gen/run.py, every replacement asserted to occur as often as it
    # says, the top summary and four blocks of the body replaced whole by their
    # anchor lines, and the body grepped afterwards for P2's names, subjects,
    # stems and the tokens pscmp, pssurvey, pagesetup and m3p3-p2. What differs,
    # and why:
    #  NA. The phase, the log directory, the subjects, the script directory
    #      (<scripts>, <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p3-p3/scripts, on the disk),
    #      the build directory (m3p3-p3/run) and the keep (m3p3-p3/keep-host) are
    #      this phase's; the base is M3 part 3 P2's record commit ("M3 part 3 P2
    #      record:"); the phase commit is P3's tool commit by its subject; the
    #      record stems are m3p3-p3- and m3p3-open-; the spec's committed blob at
    #      P3's doc commit is pinned through SPEC_SHA, planning's rulings during
    #      P3 standing uncommitted in the working tree's copy.
    #  NB. Change MB's form: the committed open-check record the keep is
    #      compared with is P2's, named by its record commit, resolved by its
    #      subject ("M3 part 3 P2 record:"), checked to be a record commit that
    #      added exactly one open-check .txt with no later commit adding another,
    #      and to be this phase's base, the parent of P3's doc commit; the
    #      control names P3's doc commit, whose subject is not a record's.
    #  NC. The comparison is pacmp.py, written for this phase on pscmp.py's
    #      readers (copied verbatim by <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p3-p3/gen/
    #      pacmp.py); the checks are --printarea-sample's (specs/0025 "Harness
    #      runs", "The calls", rulings 1 to 6 during P3), its flags listed in its
    #      docstring, printed below; --parts prints W's part and bit 3 and the
    #      workbook part's. The line's relations are the spec's: area_ok,
    #      titles_ok, filterdb_ok and hidden_ok 1, autofilter_after 1,
    #      names_after the names before plus three less those of the three W
    #      already had; the tool's counts equal the comparison's (the names and
    #      the autofilters before and after, the relationships prefix). The
    #      entries: W and xl/workbook.xml changed, every other entry identical
    #      (the calculation chain, [Content_Types].xml and the workbook's
    #      relationships among them, ruling 2); nothing added, recompressed or
    #      dropped; descriptor on each of the two exactly when its input entry
    #      sets bit 3. The edit's shapes (the autoFilter created or kept, the
    #      container created or kept, W's name bare or quoted) are printed per
    #      workbook and totalled.
    #  ND. NEW, the survey (pasurvey.py, <scripts>, copied into <work> and
    #      printed) replaces MD's: it takes <corpus> as its parameter, lists
    #      <corpus>/corpus (every regular file, no extension glob; the count
    #      checked against the manifest's rows) and prints one line per workbook
    #      (ids, counts and the class word bare or quoted; no name, reference or
    #      text): W's name class, M, W's autoFilter count, W's built-in names
    #      among the three, the workbook's names, W's tables, the overlap of a
    #      table of W with A1:H(M + 1), the calculation chain and W's
    #      relationships prefix. The log checks its forms, prints the
    #      distributions, takes the overlaps as the predicted refusals, and
    #      checks every ok line's before-figures against it.
    #  NE. Change LE (every row ok) reads, for this sample, every row ok but
    #      exactly the predicted refusals (P3: a corpus sheet whose table
    #      overlaps the area is a finding recorded with its id, not a failure):
    #      the refused ids, on each label, are the survey's overlaps, each
    #      refused with the overlap message alone; LF (the descriptor flags and
    #      the derived values, over both changed parts) and LG (TMPDIR on the
    #      disk) stand.
    #  NF. Change MF (the open check's own TMPDIR device) stands, unchanged.
    #  NG. The plants: every flag's planted control runs on the first ok
    #      workbook in manifest order whose <autoFilter> is created and on the
    #      first whose <autoFilter> is kept, as MG's, each on its own check line;
    #      a case the corpus does not hold fails its line.
    #  NH. The run loop, the record pair, the keep and the open check are MH's
    #      with this phase's names; the record is also checked to name every
    #      refused id (the record shows the refusal, P3).
    #  NI. MI stands: this script runs no `rm -rf`; the sourced
    #      scripts/counting.sh, a committed script, runs one on the directory its
    #      counting controls make (allowed: a directory the script created in
    #      that run); the working directory and the keeps stand, kept, and
    #      Python writes no bytecode.
    #
    #
    # CARRIED TO M3 part 4 P1 from M3 part 3 P3's run script (at the phase
    # commit 5c1a6b3, printed in records/logs/m3p3-p3/run.log; its change lists
    # LA to LI, MA to MI and NA to NI are above), generated by <home>/.cache/
    # emend-build/m3p4-p1/gen/run.py, every replacement asserted to occur as
    # often as it says, the top summary and five blocks of the body replaced
    # whole by their anchor lines, and the body grepped afterwards for P3's
    # names, subjects, stems and the tokens pacmp, pasurvey, printarea,
    # autoFilter, OVERLAP, predicted and m3p3-p3, with M3 part 3 P4's change OF
    # (records/logs/m3p3-p4/run.log). What differs, and why:
    #  PA. The phase, the log directory, the subjects, the script directory
    #      (<scripts>, <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p4-p1/scripts, on the disk),
    #      the build directory (m3p4-p1/run) and the keep (m3p4-p1/keep-host) are
    #      this phase's; the base is M3 part 3's close-out record commit ("M3
    #      part 3 close-out record:"); the phase commit is P1's rows_present
    #      commit by its subject (ruling 6); the record stems are m3p4-p1- and
    #      m3p4-open-; the spec is specs/0026-grouping-and-line-styles.md, its
    #      committed blob at P1's doc commit pinned through SPEC_SHA, planning's
    #      rulings during P1 standing uncommitted in the working tree's copy.
    #  PB. Change LB's form: the committed open-check record the keep is
    #      compared with is M3 part 3 P4's, the last committed, named by its
    #      record commit, resolved by its subject ("M3 part 3 P4 record:"; no
    #      hash is typed into this script), checked to be a record commit that
    #      added exactly one open-check .txt with no later commit adding
    #      another, an ancestor of the base and not the base (part 3's
    #      close-out commits came after it). The control names the base, whose
    #      subject is not P4's record's.
    #  PC. The comparison is gpcmp.py, written for this phase on pacmp.py's
    #      readers (copied); the checks are --group-sample's (specs/0026
    #      "Harness runs" and "The calls", rulings 1 to 6 during P1), its flags
    #      listed in its docstring, printed below; --parts prints W's part and
    #      its bit 3. The line's relations are the spec's (ruling 6):
    #      rows_after = rows_before + 3 - rows_present, level_rows 2,
    #      hidden_rows 2, collapsed_rows 1, max_row_ok, max_col_ok and
    #      summary_ok 1, level_cols 1 or 2; the tool's counts equal the
    #      comparison's (rows, present rows, cols, level_cols, kept_cols, the
    #      relationships prefix). The entries: W changed, every other entry
    #      identical (the calculation chain among them); nothing added,
    #      recompressed or dropped; descriptor on W exactly when its input
    #      entry sets bit 3. The edit's shapes (<sheetPr>, <sheetFormatPr>,
    #      <cols> created or kept, rows created and edited in place) are
    #      printed per workbook and totalled.
    #  PD. NEW, the survey (gpsurvey.py, <scripts>, copied into <work> and
    #      printed) replaces ND's: it takes <corpus> as its parameter, lists
    #      <corpus>/corpus (every regular file, no extension glob; the count
    #      checked against the manifest's rows) and prints one line per
    #      workbook (ids, counts and class words) and one of schema names per
    #      workbook (the shapes FACTS asks for). The log checks its forms,
    #      prints the distributions, and checks every line's before-figures
    #      against it.
    #  PE. Change LE (every row ok) stands for this sample, as it read before
    #      P3's NE: no refusal is accepted; the refusal machinery (change BK)
    #      stays to print any. LF (the descriptor flags and the derived values,
    #      over W alone) and LG (TMPDIR on the disk) stand.
    #  PF. NEW, M3 part 3 P4's change OF (specs/0025 P3 verification ruling 4):
    #      the corpus's workbooks holding xl/calcChain.xml counted by manifest
    #      order (the survey's chain column, checked against a direct zipfile
    #      count), and on each label each of their calcChain entry rows
    #      identical and unflagged, the rule that keeps the chain named in one
    #      line.
    #  PG. NEW, ruling 3: the input <col> elements covering column 2 or 3 that
    #      carry hidden="1", which the group removes, counted per workbook by
    #      the comparison and totalled per label, checked against the survey's;
    #      and those carrying a hidden attribute of any value (LibreOffice
    #      writes hidden="false"), which the write drops as well, since it
    #      removes the attribute whatever its value, counted the same way.
    #  PH. Change MF (the open check's own TMPDIR device) stands, unchanged.
    #  PI. The plants: every flag's planted control runs on the first ok
    #      workbook in manifest order whose <sheetPr> is created and on the
    #      first whose <sheetPr> is kept, as NG's, each on its own check line;
    #      a case the corpus does not hold fails its line.
    #  PJ. The run loop, the record pair, the keep and the open check are NH's
    #      with this phase's names; NH's check that the record names every
    #      refused id is dropped with the refusals (PE).
    #  PK. NI stands: this script runs no `rm -rf`; the sourced
    #      scripts/counting.sh, a committed script, runs one on the directory its
    #      counting controls make (allowed: a directory the script created in
    #      that run); the working directory and the keeps stand, kept, and
    #      Python writes no bytecode.
    #
    # Usage: m3p4-p1-run.sh <phase commit> <this phase's test.log> > <file>
    set -uo pipefail
    SELF_DIR=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
    SELF=$SELF_DIR/$(basename "$0")
    # specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7: this script's own standard error, kept and counted at the end.
    mkdir -p "$SELF_DIR/out" || exit 2
    ERR=$SELF_DIR/out/run.stderr
    exec 2>"$ERR"
    cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" || exit 2
    MAIN=$(pwd)
    . scripts/counting.sh
    
    C=${1:?phase commit required}
    TEST_LOG=${2:?this phase test.log required}
    # Change AS: every environment input, as it was set, before any is unset.
    INPUT_NAMES="SPEC_SHA RUN_SUFFIX SUPERSEDED_RUN SUPERSEDED_KEEP RERUN_NOTE RERUN_FILES RECORDS_DEST RUN_KEEP RUN_BUILD_ROOT RUN_OUT_ROOT RUN_SKIP_KEEP EMEND_CORPUS_DIR HOME ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"
    declare -A INPUT_SEEN
    for v in $INPUT_NAMES; do
      if [ -n "${!v+x}" ]; then INPUT_SEEN[$v]=${!v}; else INPUT_SEEN[$v]=unset; fi
      # Change BL (part 4a P3's AW): the key's value is never printed, only whether it is set.
      if [ "$v" = ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ] && [ "${INPUT_SEEN[$v]}" != unset ]; then INPUT_SEEN[$v]="set (value not printed)"; fi
    done
    CORPUS=${EMEND_CORPUS_DIR:-$HOME/emend-testing}
    export RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0 CARGO_TERM_COLOR=never CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=4
    # Change JI: Python writes no bytecode, so nothing arises to be removed.
    export PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1
    unset EMEND_KEEP_DIR EMEND_CORPUS_DIR
    IMAGE=localhost/emend-lo:25.2.3-2-deb13u6
    LO_TIMEOUT_S=600
    SPEC=specs/0026-grouping-and-line-styles.md
    SPEC_SHA=${SPEC_SHA:-}
    if [ -z "$SPEC_SHA" ]; then echo "SPEC_SHA, the spec's sha256, is a required input (change AR)" >&2; exit 2; fi
    EDIT=--group-sample
    # The logged run leaves RUN_BUILD_ROOT and RUN_KEEP unset; a dry run points
    # them elsewhere so it leaves no keep where the logged run refuses one.
    BUILD_ROOT=${RUN_BUILD_ROOT:-$HOME/.cache/emend-build/m3p4-p1/run}
    KEEP=${RUN_KEEP:-$HOME/.cache/emend-build/m3p4-p1/keep-host}
    # Change JE (M3 part 1 P3's ID): the dry-run inputs.
    RUN_OUT_ROOT=${RUN_OUT_ROOT:-$CORPUS/runs}
    RUN_SKIP_KEEP=${RUN_SKIP_KEEP:-no}
    case $RUN_SKIP_KEEP in yes | no) ;; *) echo "RUN_SKIP_KEEP is yes or no" >&2; exit 2 ;; esac
    INSTALLED=()
    I686=i686-unknown-linux-musl
    # Change AK: where the record pairs are installed.
    RECORDS_DEST=${RECORDS_DEST:-records}
    # Change I: a keep in place is another attempt's, moved below once the
    # header can list it; without SUPERSEDED_KEEP naming the attempt it is
    # refused.
    SUPERSEDED_KEEP=${SUPERSEDED_KEEP:-}
    case $SUPERSEDED_KEEP in '' | attempt-[1-9]) ;; *) echo "SUPERSEDED_KEEP is attempt-<n> or nothing" >&2; exit 2 ;; esac
    if [ "$RUN_SKIP_KEEP" = no ] && [ -e "$KEEP" ] && [ -z "$SUPERSEDED_KEEP" ]; then echo "$KEEP is already there; name its attempt in SUPERSEDED_KEEP" >&2; exit 2; fi
    mkdir -p "$BUILD_ROOT" || exit 2
    export CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$BUILD_ROOT/target
    RECORDS=$SELF_DIR/out/records
    # Change JI: the working directory is on the disk under <scripts>/out and
    # kept; nothing here is removed.
    B=$(mktemp -d "$SELF_DIR/out/work.XXXXXX") || exit 2
    fail=0
    check() { echo "  $1: $2"; [ "$2" = yes ] || fail=1; }
    yn() { if "$@"; then echo yes; else echo no; fi; }
    TAB=$(printf '\t')
    sha_of() { sha256sum <"$1" | cut -d' ' -f1; }
    
    head_is() { [ "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" = "$1" ]; }
    not_head() { if head_is "$1"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    full_sha() { printf '%s' "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE '^[0-9a-f]{40}$'; }
    if full_sha "$C"; then :; else echo "the phase commit must be a full 40-hex sha, not $C" >&2; exit 2; fi
    if head_is "$C"; then :; else echo "HEAD is not $C" >&2; exit 2; fi
    NULL_SHA=0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
    SHORT=$(git rev-parse --short=7 "$C")
    # Change CE (P3's BZ): planning's uncommitted rulings in specs/0026 are the one
    # planning file the status allows, as a modified tracked file (change MA).
    OURS='^((\?\?| ?[MARCD]) records/logs/m3p4-p1|(\?\?| ?[MARCD]) records/m3p4-(p1|open)-2[^ ]*-'"$SHORT"'[.](md|txt)$| M specs/0026-grouping-and-line-styles[.]md$)'
    entry_all=$(run_lines git status --porcelain)
    entry_ours=$(run_matches -E "$OURS" git status --porcelain)
    entry_clean() { [ "$entry_all" != error ] && [ "$entry_ours" != error ] && [ "$entry_all" = "$entry_ours" ]; }
    if entry_clean; then :; else
      echo "the working tree holds changes outside this phase's records and planning's spec" >&2
      exit 2
    fi
    DATE=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%d)
    STEM_OPEN=m3p4-open-$DATE-$SHORT
    STEM_RUN=m3p4-p1-$DATE-$SHORT
    # A rerun takes a suffix, so its run directory is never the superseded one.
    RUN_SUFFIX=${RUN_SUFFIX:-}
    case $RUN_SUFFIX in '' | -[b-z]) ;; *) echo "RUN_SUFFIX is -b to -z or nothing" >&2; exit 2 ;; esac
    RUN=$DATE-$SHORT$RUN_SUFFIX
    OUT=$RUN_OUT_ROOT/$RUN
    mkdir -p "$RECORDS" "$RECORDS_DEST" || exit 2
    # A rerun names the superseded run directory, which is MOVED into
    # <scripts>/out/superseded after the header prints it, never removed; it
    # must be another run of this phase, not this one.
    SUPERSEDED_RUN=${SUPERSEDED_RUN:-}
    case $SUPERSEDED_RUN in
      '' | 20[0-9][0-9]-[01][0-9]-[0-3][0-9]-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f] | 20[0-9][0-9]-[01][0-9]-[0-3][0-9]-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]-[b-z]) ;;
      *) echo "SUPERSEDED_RUN is not a run directory's name" >&2; exit 2 ;;
    esac
    if [ -n "$SUPERSEDED_RUN" ] && [ "$SUPERSEDED_RUN" = "$RUN" ]; then echo "SUPERSEDED_RUN names this run's own directory" >&2; exit 2; fi
    SUP_OUT=$RUN_OUT_ROOT/$SUPERSEDED_RUN
    SUP_TO=$SELF_DIR/out/superseded/run-$SUPERSEDED_RUN
    for f in "$OUT" "$RECORDS/$STEM_OPEN.md" "$RECORDS/$STEM_OPEN.txt" "$RECORDS_DEST/$STEM_OPEN.md" "$RECORDS_DEST/$STEM_OPEN.txt" \
             "$RECORDS/$STEM_RUN.md" "$RECORDS/$STEM_RUN.txt" "$RECORDS_DEST/$STEM_RUN.md" "$RECORDS_DEST/$STEM_RUN.txt"; do
      if [ -e "$f" ]; then echo "$f is already there; move it aside first" >&2; exit 2; fi
    done
    # A run directory with a summary for either label before the runner starts
    # is another attempt's (memory: a same-day rerun reads the previous attempt's
    # files); refused here, before the runner, with the exact message.
    for sl in host i686; do
      if [ -e "$OUT/summary.$sl.tsv" ]; then echo "$OUT/summary.$sl.tsv is already there" >&2; exit 2; fi
    done
    
    scrub() {
      sed -e "s#$MAIN#<repo>#g" -e "s#$B#<work>#g" -e "s#$SELF_DIR#<scripts>#g" -e "s#$KEEP#<keep>#g" \
        -e "s#$BUILD_ROOT#<build>#g" -e "s#$RUN_OUT_ROOT#<runs>#g" -e "s#$CORPUS#<corpus>#g" -e "s#$HOME#<home>#g"
    }
    exec 3>&1
    exec > >(scrub >&3)
    SCRUB_PID=$!
    
    echo "command: git rev-parse HEAD"
    echo "invocation: bash <scripts>/$(basename "$0") $*"
    echo "about: M3 part 4 P1 phase commit $C; HEAD at run: $(git rev-parse HEAD)"
    # Change AS: the environment inputs, each on its labelled line.
    for v in $INPUT_NAMES; do echo "input: $v=${INPUT_SEEN[$v]}"; done
    echo
    echo "## the three shape greps, over this script, before its log (specs/0001)"
    D='$'
    SHAPE_CHAIN="\\${D}\\((yn|is|isnot) .*(&&|\\|\\|)"
    SHAPE_BANG="\\${D}\\((yn|is|isnot) !"
    SHAPE_ASSIGN="\\${D}\\((yn|is|isnot) [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*="
    printf '%s\n' "x=${D}(is [ 1 ] && true)" "y=${D}(isnot ! true)" "z=${D}(yn N=1 true)" >"$B/shape-fixture"
    echo "command: count_matches -E <shape> <this script>, and the same over a fixture holding one line of each shape"
    for shape in CHAIN BANG ASSIGN; do
      var=SHAPE_$shape
      n_self=$(count_matches -E "${!var}" "$SELF")
      n_fix=$(count_matches -E "${!var}" "$B/shape-fixture")
      echo "  shape $shape: in this script $n_self; in the fixture $n_fix"
      check "$shape: this script holds none" "$(yn [ "$n_self" = 0 ])"
      check "control: $shape: the same form finds the fixture's one line" "$(yn [ "$n_fix" = 1 ])"
    done
    
    echo
    echo "## the phase's commits by role, read from git"
    by_subject() { git log --format='%H' -n 1 -F --grep="$1"; }
    REC=$(by_subject 'M3 part 3 close-out record:')
    CODE=$(by_subject "M3 part 4 P1: the group sample's rows_present")
    DOC=$(by_subject 'M3 part 4 P1: commit planning docs')
    # Change PB: the record the keep is compared with, named by its record
    # commit, resolved by its subject (no hash is typed here), and checked below;
    # an ancestor of the base, not the base.
    PREV_OPEN_REC=$(by_subject 'M3 part 3 P4 record:')
    echo "command: git log --format=%H -n 1 -F --grep=<the role's subject>, for each role"
    echo "  M3 part 3's close-out record commit (the base): ${REC:-none}"
    echo "  P1's doc commit: ${DOC:-none}"
    echo "  the rows_present commit, the phase commit: ${CODE:-none}"
    echo "  M3 part 3 P4's record commit, the last to add an open-check record, named by its commit (changes CC, JB, LB, MB, NB and PB): ${PREV_OPEN_REC:-none}"
    echo "command: git log -1 --format=%s $PREV_OPEN_REC"
    echo "    $(git log -1 --format=%s "$PREV_OPEN_REC")"
    prev_is_record() { [ -n "$PREV_OPEN_REC" ] && git cat-file -e "$PREV_OPEN_REC^{commit}" && [ "$(git log -1 --format=%s "$PREV_OPEN_REC" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -cE '^M3 part 3 P4 record: ')" = 1 ] && git merge-base --is-ancestor "$PREV_OPEN_REC" "$C"; }
    check "the named record commit is M3 part 3 P4's record commit, an ancestor of the phase commit" "$(yn prev_is_record)"
    prev_before_base() { [ -n "$REC" ] && [ "$PREV_OPEN_REC" != "$REC" ] && git merge-base --is-ancestor "$PREV_OPEN_REC" "$REC" && [ "$(git rev-parse "$DOC^")" = "$REC" ]; }
    check "the named record commit is an ancestor of the base, not the base, and the base is the parent of P1's doc commit (change PB)" "$(yn prev_before_base)"
    prev_ctl() { local PREV_OPEN_REC=$REC; if prev_is_record; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: the same check refuses the base named instead" "$(yn prev_ctl)"
    check "the phase commit given to this script is a full sha" "$(yn full_sha "$C")"
    check "the phase commit given to this script is HEAD" "$(yn head_is "$C")"
    check "the phase commit is the tool commit, by its subject" "$(yn [ "$CODE" = "$C" ])"
    check "control: the same comparison against the null commit says no" "$(yn not_head "$NULL_SHA")"
    check "control: not_head says no for HEAD itself, so it can fail" "$(yn [ "$(yn not_head "$C")" = no ])"
    echo "phase: Milestone 3 part 4 P1 (specs/0026-grouping-and-line-styles.md) run.log; run at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
    if [ -n "${RERUN_NOTE:-}" ]; then
      echo "rerun: $RERUN_NOTE"
      echo "command: sha256sum and wc -c over each superseded attempt named above, with the directory it is kept in (change AT)"
      for sf in ${RERUN_FILES:-}; do
        if [ -f "$sf" ]; then
          printf '    %s  %s bytes  %s  kept in %s\n' "$(sha256sum "$sf" | cut -d' ' -f1)" "$(wc -c <"$sf")" "$(basename "$sf")" "$(dirname "$sf")"
        else
          printf '    NO HASH EXISTS for %s: the file is not there at run time (named in %s)\n' "$(basename "$sf")" "$(dirname "$sf")"
        fi
      done
      if [ -z "${RERUN_FILES:-}" ]; then echo "    RERUN_FILES was not set, so no attempt above is hashed by this run"; fi
    fi
    
    # Change AI: the two move checks as functions, run over planted inputs every
    # time below, and over a real moved keep or run directory when there is one.
    # keep_pairs_ok <listing>: the .in.xlsx lines times two equal the listing's
    # lines (P2 ruling 14 of specs/0018; the pattern in double quotes so the tab
    # is interpolated).
    keep_pairs_ok() {
      local pairs files
      pairs=$(count_matches -E "[.]in[.]xlsx${TAB}" "$1")
      files=$(count_lines "$1")
      [ "$files" -ge 2 ] && [ "$((pairs * 2))" = "$files" ]
    }
    # run_listing <dir> <listing>: the listing of a run directory, one line per
    # file, path and bytes (specs/0018 P2 verification ruling 4's form).
    run_listing() { (cd "$1" && find . -type f -printf '%P\t%s\n' | LC_ALL=C sort) >"$2"; }
    # run_listing_ok <dir> <listing>: the listing names each file once and at
    # least one.
    run_listing_ok() {
      local files lines uniq
      files=$(find "$1" -type f | wc -l)
      lines=$(count_lines "$2")
      uniq=$(cut -f1 "$2" | LC_ALL=C sort -u | count_lines /dev/stdin)
      [ "$files" -ge 1 ] && [ "$lines" = "$files" ] && [ "$uniq" = "$files" ]
    }
    
    if [ -n "$SUPERSEDED_RUN" ]; then
      echo "the superseded run directory, moved before this run: <runs>/$SUPERSEDED_RUN to <scripts>/out/superseded/run-$SUPERSEDED_RUN"
      if [ -d "$SUP_OUT" ]; then
        echo "command: sha256sum <runs>/$SUPERSEDED_RUN/summary.host.tsv and summary.i686.tsv; mv <runs>/$SUPERSEDED_RUN <scripts>/out/superseded/run-$SUPERSEDED_RUN"
        for sl in host i686; do
          if [ -f "$SUP_OUT/summary.$sl.tsv" ]; then echo "    summary.$sl.tsv sha256 $(sha_of "$SUP_OUT/summary.$sl.tsv")"; else echo "    summary.$sl.tsv: NO HASH EXISTS, the file is not there"; fi
        done
        run_listing "$SUP_OUT" "$B/superseded-run.listing"
        echo "command: (cd <runs>/$SUPERSEDED_RUN && find . -type f -printf '%P<tab>%s<newline>' | LC_ALL=C sort) | sha256sum"
        echo "    files $(find "$SUP_OUT" -type f | wc -l); listing lines $(count_lines "$B/superseded-run.listing"); listing sha256 $(sha_of "$B/superseded-run.listing")"
        check "the listing of $SUPERSEDED_RUN names each of its files once" "$(yn run_listing_ok "$SUP_OUT" "$B/superseded-run.listing")"
        mkdir -p "$SELF_DIR/out/superseded" && mv "$SUP_OUT" "$SUP_TO"
      fi
      sup_moved() { [ ! -e "$SUP_OUT" ] && [ -d "$SUP_TO" ]; }
      check "the superseded run directory is moved, not removed, before the run" "$(yn sup_moved)"
    fi
    if [ -n "$SUPERSEDED_KEEP" ]; then
      KEEP_TO=$SELF_DIR/out/superseded/keep-$SUPERSEDED_KEEP
      echo "the superseded keep (change I), moved before this run: <keep> to <scripts>/out/superseded/keep-$SUPERSEDED_KEEP"
      if [ -d "$KEEP" ]; then
        (cd "$KEEP" && find . -type f -printf '%P\t%s\n' | LC_ALL=C sort) >"$B/superseded-keep.listing"
        echo "command: (cd <keep> && find . -type f -printf '%P<tab>%s<newline>' | LC_ALL=C sort) | sha256sum; the .in.xlsx files counted; mv <keep> <scripts>/out/superseded/keep-$SUPERSEDED_KEEP"
        echo "    pairs $(count_matches -E "[.]in[.]xlsx${TAB}" "$B/superseded-keep.listing"); files $(count_lines "$B/superseded-keep.listing"); listing sha256 $(sha_of "$B/superseded-keep.listing")"
        check "the moved keep's pairs times two equals its files" "$(yn keep_pairs_ok "$B/superseded-keep.listing")"
        if [ -e "$KEEP_TO" ]; then echo "    $KEEP_TO is already there"; fail=1; else mkdir -p "$SELF_DIR/out/superseded" && mv "$KEEP" "$KEEP_TO"; fi
      else
        echo "    NO LISTING EXISTS: there is no keep in place to move"
      fi
      keep_moved() { [ ! -e "$KEEP" ] && [ -d "$KEEP_TO" ]; }
      check "the superseded keep is moved, not removed, before the run" "$(yn keep_moved)"
    fi
    echo "superseded run directory named: ${SUPERSEDED_RUN:-none}; superseded keep named: ${SUPERSEDED_KEEP:-none}"
    echo
    echo "## the two move checks over planted inputs, run every time (change AI)"
    printf 'x.1.in.xlsx%s1\nx.1.out.xlsx%s1\n' "$TAB" "$TAB" >"$B/c-keep.listing"
    printf 'x.1.in.xlsx%s1\nx.1.out.xlsx%s1\ny.1.out.xlsx%s1\n' "$TAB" "$TAB" "$TAB" >"$B/c-keep-odd.listing"
    echo "  planted keep listing: pairs $(count_matches -E "[.]in[.]xlsx${TAB}" "$B/c-keep.listing"), files $(count_lines "$B/c-keep.listing"); with an unpaired output: pairs $(count_matches -E "[.]in[.]xlsx${TAB}" "$B/c-keep-odd.listing"), files $(count_lines "$B/c-keep-odd.listing")"
    check "keep_pairs_ok passes a planted listing of one whole pair" "$(yn keep_pairs_ok "$B/c-keep.listing")"
    kp_ctl() { if keep_pairs_ok "$B/c-keep-odd.listing"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: keep_pairs_ok refuses a planted listing with an unpaired output" "$(yn kp_ctl)"
    mkdir -p "$B/c-run/abc123" && printf 'a' >"$B/c-run/summary.host.tsv" && printf 'bb' >"$B/c-run/abc123/out.host.xlsx" && printf 'ccc' >"$B/c-run/abc123/stdout.host.txt"
    run_listing "$B/c-run" "$B/c-run.listing"
    echo "  planted run directory: files $(find "$B/c-run" -type f | wc -l); listing lines $(count_lines "$B/c-run.listing"); listing sha256 $(sha_of "$B/c-run.listing")"
    check "run_listing_ok passes the planted run directory's own listing" "$(yn run_listing_ok "$B/c-run" "$B/c-run.listing")"
    { cat "$B/c-run.listing"; head -n 1 "$B/c-run.listing"; } >"$B/c-run-dup.listing"
    rl_ctl() { if run_listing_ok "$B/c-run" "$B/c-run-dup.listing"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: run_listing_ok refuses a listing that names one file twice" "$(yn rl_ctl)"
    n_cargo=$(pgrep -x cargo | wc -l)
    n_rustc=$(pgrep -x rustc | wc -l)
    echo "SERIALIZED: no other log run was in flight; cargo processes at entry: $n_cargo; rustc processes at entry: $n_rustc; this run used its own target directory, <build>/target (CARGO_TARGET_DIR)"
    check "no cargo or rustc process was running at entry" "$(yn [ "$((n_cargo + n_rustc))" = 0 ])"
    echo "DETACHED: no interactive call waits on this run; stdout and stderr go to a file, polled from later calls."
    echo "TIMEOUT CHOSEN BEFORE THE RUN: --timeout 300 for the copy child and --lo-timeout $LO_TIMEOUT_S per conversion, the figures every corpus run of this milestone used; not tuned during the run."
    echo "root: <repo> stands for the repository's top level (inside <home>, so scrubbed first); scripts/counting.sh is sourced from it by this log; scripts/passthrough-run.sh, scripts/passthrough-record.py and scripts/edit-open-check.sh are run from it, and the runner and the open check each source scripts/lo-check.sh, which is never run; the two record pairs are installed into its $RECORDS_DEST/; the test.log given is read from it"
    echo "root: <home> stands for the home directory of the account that ran this script"
    echo "root: <scripts> stands for <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p4-p1/scripts on the disk, this script's own directory, which holds the script, gpcmp.py and gpsurvey.py beside it; the two record pairs are written into <scripts>/out/records first, a superseded run directory and a superseded keep are moved into <scripts>/out/superseded, and this script's own standard error goes to <scripts>/out/run.stderr (specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7)"
    echo "root: <work> stands for this run's working directory, made by mktemp -d under <scripts>/out on the disk (the comparison and the survey copied from beside this script, their outputs, derived tables, the planted listings and run directory, the runs' TMPDIR <work>/tmp-run (change LG), the open check's TMPDIR <work>/tmp, the i686 keep's listing), kept after the run and never removed (change JI)"
    echo "root: <build> stands for <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p4-p1/run on the disk: <build>/target the builds (release binaries and tests), <build>/keep-i686.<pid> the i686 keep, kept after the comparison (change JI)"
    echo "root: <keep> stands for <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p4-p1/keep-host on the disk, this phase's host keep; kept after the run for planning"
    echo "root: <corpus> stands for the private corpus directory (the manifest and the inputs under <corpus>/corpus, read)"
    echo "root: <runs> stands for the corpus run directories' parent, <corpus>/runs unless RUN_OUT_ROOT names another for a dry run (change JE); this log's run directory <runs>/$RUN is written there"
    apart() { case "$1/" in "$2"/*) return 1 ;; esac; case "$2/" in "$1"/*) return 1 ;; esac; return 0; }
    roots_distinct() {
      local a b all=("$SELF_DIR" "$BUILD_ROOT" "$MAIN" "$KEEP" "$CORPUS")
      for a in "${all[@]}"; do for b in "${all[@]}"; do
        [ "$a" = "$b" ] && continue
        apart "$a" "$b" || return 1
      done; done
    }
    check "the roots other than <home>, <work> and <runs> are distinct, none inside another" "$(yn roots_distinct)"
    work_in_scripts() { case "$B/" in "$SELF_DIR/out/"*) return 0 ;; esac; return 1; }
    check "<work> is under <scripts>/out on the disk (change JI)" "$(yn work_in_scripts)"
    work_ctl() { local B=/tmp/x; if work_in_scripts; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: the same test refuses a working directory under /tmp" "$(yn work_ctl)"
    runs_apart() { apart "$RUN_OUT_ROOT" "$MAIN" && apart "$RUN_OUT_ROOT" "$SELF_DIR"; }
    check "<runs> lies outside <repo> and <scripts>" "$(yn runs_apart)"
    roots_ctl() { if apart "$CARGO_TARGET_DIR" "$BUILD_ROOT"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: apart refuses <build>/target against <build>, which holds it" "$(yn roots_ctl)"
    echo "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY set in this shell: $([ -n "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ] && echo yes || echo no)"
    check "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is not set" "$(yn [ -z "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ])"
    echo "the run directory: <runs>/$RUN; the record stems: $STEM_RUN and $STEM_OPEN; the records' destination: $RECORDS_DEST; RUN_SKIP_KEEP: $RUN_SKIP_KEEP"
    echo "at entry: status lines $entry_all; of them this phase's records or planning's spec $entry_ours; the lines:"
    git status --porcelain | sed 's/^/    /'
    echo
    echo "## script that wrote this log"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$SELF"
    echo
    echo "## the shared counting library this log sources"
    sed 's/^/    /' scripts/counting.sh
    echo
    echo "## counting controls"
    counting_controls
    if [ "$counting_controls_ok" != yes ]; then fail=1; fi
    
    echo
    echo "## the scripts, against the phase commit, and planning's uncommitted spec"
    tree_is_commit() { [ "$(sha_of "$1")" = "$(git show "$C:$1" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)" ]; }
    for s in scripts/passthrough-run.sh scripts/passthrough-record.py scripts/lo-check.sh scripts/edit-open-check.sh; do
      check "$s in the main tree is the phase commit's (sha256 $(sha_of "$s"))" "$(yn tree_is_commit "$s")"
    done
    tree_ctl() { if [ "$(git show "$C:scripts/excel-check-list.py" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)" = "$(sha_of scripts/edit-open-check.sh)" ]; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: the same hash comparison tells two different scripts apart" "$(yn tree_ctl)"
    # Change CE (P3's BZ): the pin is the committed spec; the working tree's copy
    # holds planning's uncommitted rulings during P1 and is printed, not pinned.
    spec_now=$(sha_of "$SPEC")
    spec_committed=$(git show "$C:$SPEC" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)
    spec_doc=$(git show "$(by_subject 'M3 part 4 P1: commit planning docs'):$SPEC" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)
    echo "  the spec: $SPEC; at the phase commit sha256 $spec_committed; at the doc commit $spec_doc; the pin, the input SPEC_SHA: $SPEC_SHA"
    echo "  the working tree's copy (planning's uncommitted rulings during P1, change CE): sha256 $spec_now"
    spec_ok() { [ "$spec_committed" = "$SPEC_SHA" ]; }
    check "the spec at the phase commit is at the one pinned hash" "$(yn spec_ok)"
    check "the spec at the phase commit is the doc commit's" "$(yn [ "$spec_committed" = "$spec_doc" ])"
    spec_ctl() { local spec_committed=1111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111; if spec_ok; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: the same check refuses the spec against another hash" "$(yn spec_ctl)"
    echo "command: podman image exists $IMAGE"
    check "the pinned LibreOffice image is there" "$(yn podman image exists "$IMAGE")"
    echo
    echo "## the release binaries, built here at the phase commit, both targets"
    echo "command: cargo build --release -p emend-copy -p xlsx-diff; the same with --target $I686"
    cargo build --release -p emend-copy -p xlsx-diff >"$B/build-host.out" 2>&1 </dev/null
    rc_h=$?
    cargo build --release -p emend-copy -p xlsx-diff --target "$I686" >"$B/build-i686.out" 2>&1 </dev/null
    rc_i=$?
    echo "  exit: host $rc_h, $I686 $rc_i"
    check "both release builds exit 0" "$(yn [ "$((rc_h + rc_i))" = 0 ])"
    PT_host=$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release/emend-copy
    XD_host=$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release/xlsx-diff
    PT_i686=$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/$I686/release/emend-copy
    XD_i686=$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/$I686/release/xlsx-diff
    for b in "$PT_host" "$XD_host" "$PT_i686" "$XD_i686"; do echo "  $b: sha256 $(sha_of "$b"), bytes $(stat -c %s "$b")"; done
    echo "  $(rustc --version)"
    
    
    echo
    echo
    echo "## the survey of the corpus before the run (change PD)"
    cp "$SELF_DIR/gpsurvey.py" "$B/gpsurvey.py" || exit 2
    echo "command: cp <scripts>/gpsurvey.py <work>/gpsurvey.py; sed 's/^/    /' <work>/gpsurvey.py; sha256 $(sha_of "$B/gpsurvey.py"), $(wc -c <"$B/gpsurvey.py") bytes"
    check "the copy is the file beside this script, byte for byte" "$(yn cmp -s "$SELF_DIR/gpsurvey.py" "$B/gpsurvey.py")"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/gpsurvey.py"
    echo "command: python3 <work>/gpsurvey.py <corpus> (wb: id, M, rows, present, cols, sheetPr, outlinePr, fmt, maxrow, maxcol, cover, hidden, chain, r bound, hidden any; names: id and three shapes; then files; tab-separated)"
    python3 "$B/gpsurvey.py" "$CORPUS" >"$B/survey.out" 2>"$B/survey.err"
    src=$?
    echo "  exit: $src; stderr bytes: $(wc -c <"$B/survey.err"); lines: $(count_lines "$B/survey.out")"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/survey.out"
    survey_ran() { [ "$src" = 0 ] && [ ! -s "$B/survey.err" ]; }
    check "the survey exits 0 with an empty stderr" "$(yn survey_ran)"
    manifest_rows=$(awk -F'\t' 'NR > 1 { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$CORPUS/manifest.tsv")
    SV_FILES=$(awk -F'\t' '$1 == "files" { print $2 }' "$B/survey.out")
    SV_ROWS=$(awk -F'\t' '$1 == "files" { print $3 }' "$B/survey.out")
    SV_READ=$(awk -F'\t' '$1 == "files" { print $4 }' "$B/survey.out")
    SV_WB=$(awk -F'\t' '$1 == "wb" && NF == 16 { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$B/survey.out")
    SV_NAMES=$(awk -F'\t' '$1 == "names" && NF == 5 { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$B/survey.out")
    echo "  corpus manifest rows: $manifest_rows; the survey's regular files under <corpus>/corpus: $SV_FILES; its manifest rows: $SV_ROWS; workbooks read: $SV_READ; full wb lines: $SV_WB; full names lines: $SV_NAMES"
    check "the corpus holds its 27 workbooks" "$(yn [ "$manifest_rows" = 27 ])"
    survey_whole() { [ "$SV_FILES" = "$manifest_rows" ] && [ "$SV_ROWS" = "$manifest_rows" ] && [ "$SV_READ" = "$manifest_rows" ] && [ "$SV_WB" = "$manifest_rows" ] && [ "$SV_NAMES" = "$manifest_rows" ]; }
    check "the survey listed one regular file per manifest row and read every workbook with one full wb line and one names line each" "$(yn survey_whole)"
    # survey_forms_ok <survey output>: every wb line has sixteen fields, every
    # count a number, the maximums' classes words of the survey's four, present
    # 0 to 3, the hidden covering elements (hidden="1", and a hidden attribute
    # of any value) no more than the covering ones, the flags 0 or 1; at least
    # one line.
    survey_forms_ok() {
      awk -F'\t' '
        $1 == "wb" {
          nw++
          if (NF != 16) { bad++; next }
          for (col = 3; col <= 9; col++) if ($col !~ /^[0-9]+$/) bad++
          for (col = 12; col <= 16; col++) if ($col !~ /^[0-9]+$/) bad++
          if ($10 !~ /^(absent|zero|one-up|other)$/ || $11 !~ /^(absent|zero|one-up|other)$/) bad++
          if ($5 > 3 || $13 > $12 || $16 > $12 || $13 > $16) bad++
          if ($14 !~ /^[01]$/ || $15 !~ /^[01]$/) bad++
        }
        END { exit (nw > 0 && bad == 0) ? 0 : 1 }' "$1"
    }
    check "every surveyed line has the survey's form, at most three rows present after M, no more hidden covering elements than covering ones" "$(yn survey_forms_ok "$B/survey.out")"
    for planted in "wb${TAB}x${TAB}1${TAB}1${TAB}4${TAB}0${TAB}1${TAB}0${TAB}1${TAB}zero${TAB}zero${TAB}1${TAB}0${TAB}0${TAB}1${TAB}0" \
                   "wb${TAB}x${TAB}1${TAB}1${TAB}0${TAB}0${TAB}1${TAB}0${TAB}1${TAB}some${TAB}zero${TAB}1${TAB}0${TAB}0${TAB}1${TAB}0" \
                   "wb${TAB}x${TAB}1${TAB}1${TAB}0${TAB}0${TAB}1${TAB}0${TAB}1${TAB}zero${TAB}zero${TAB}1${TAB}2${TAB}0${TAB}1${TAB}2" \
                   "wb${TAB}x${TAB}1${TAB}1${TAB}0${TAB}0${TAB}1${TAB}0${TAB}1${TAB}zero${TAB}zero${TAB}1${TAB}0${TAB}0${TAB}1${TAB}2" \
                   "wb${TAB}x${TAB}1${TAB}1${TAB}0"; do
      { cat "$B/survey.out"; printf '%s\n' "$planted"; } >"$B/c-survey"
      sv_ctl() { if survey_forms_ok "$B/c-survey"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
      check "control: survey_forms_ok refuses the survey with a planted line ($(printf '%s' "$planted" | cut -f3- | tr '\t' ' '))" "$(yn sv_ctl)"
    done
    printf 'wb\tx\t5\t9\t3\t2\t1\t0\t1\tone-up\tother\t2\t2\t1\t1\t2\nwb\ty\t0\t0\t0\t0\t0\t0\t0\tabsent\tabsent\t0\t0\t0\t0\t0\n' >"$B/c-survey-ok"
    check "control: survey_forms_ok accepts planted lines of every allowed form" "$(yn survey_forms_ok "$B/c-survey-ok")"
    echo "  the shapes over the corpus (rows and M shown as 0 or more than 0):"
    awk -F'\t' '$1 == "wb" { print "present " $5 " cols " ($6 > 0 ? "some" : "none") " sheetPr " $7 " outlinePr " $8 " fmt " $9 " maxrow " $10 " maxcol " $11 " cover " $12 " hidden " $13 " chain " $14 " r_bound " $15 " hidden_any " $16 }' "$B/survey.out" | LC_ALL=C sort | uniq -c | sed 's/^/    /'
    echo "  the shapes as names (<sheetPr>'s children, <sheetFormatPr>'s attributes, the covering <col> elements' attributes):"
    awk -F'\t' '$1 == "names" { print "sheetPr " $3 " fmt " $4 " cover " $5 }' "$B/survey.out" | LC_ALL=C sort | uniq -c | sed 's/^/    /'
    SV_PRESENT=$(awk -F'\t' '$1 == "wb" { n += $5 } END { print n + 0 }' "$B/survey.out")
    SV_HIDDEN=$(awk -F'\t' '$1 == "wb" { n += $13 } END { print n + 0 }' "$B/survey.out")
    SV_HIDDEN_WB=$(awk -F'\t' '$1 == "wb" && $13 > 0 { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$B/survey.out")
    echo "  rows numbered M + 1 to M + 3 already present, over the corpus (ruling 6): $SV_PRESENT, in $(awk -F'\t' '$1 == "wb" && $5 > 0 { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$B/survey.out") workbooks"
    echo "  <col> elements covering column 2 or 3 with hidden=\"1\", which the group removes (ruling 3): $SV_HIDDEN, in $SV_HIDDEN_WB workbooks"
    SV_HIDDEN_ANY=$(awk -F'\t' '$1 == "wb" { n += $16 } END { print n + 0 }' "$B/survey.out")
    echo "  <col> elements covering column 2 or 3 with a hidden attribute of any value (LibreOffice writes hidden=\"false\"), which the group drops as well: $SV_HIDDEN_ANY, in $(awk -F'\t' '$1 == "wb" && $16 > 0 { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$B/survey.out") workbooks"
    # surveyed <id> <column>: the survey's wb field for the workbook.
    surveyed() { awk -F'\t' -v id="$1" -v c="$2" '$1 == "wb" && $2 == id { print $c }' "$B/survey.out"; }
    
    echo
    echo "## the corpus manifest, and its workbooks holding a calculation chain (change PF; specs/0025 P3 verification ruling 4)"
    awk -F'\t' '$1 == "wb" && $14 == 1 { print $2 }' "$B/survey.out" >"$B/chain-ids"
    awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) k[$i] = i; next } { print $k["id"] "\t" $k["ext"] }' "$CORPUS/manifest.tsv" >"$B/order"
    # chain_direct: the same count by zipfile, one call per manifest row.
    : >"$B/chain-direct"
    while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do
      if [ "$(python3 -c 'import sys, zipfile; print(1 if "xl/calcChain.xml" in zipfile.ZipFile(sys.argv[1]).namelist() else 0)' "$CORPUS/corpus/$id.$ext")" = 1 ]; then
        printf '%s\n' "$id" >>"$B/chain-direct"
      fi
    done <"$B/order"
    N_CHAIN=$(count_lines "$B/chain-ids")
    echo "command: the survey's chain column; python3 -c <zipfile namelist> <corpus>/corpus/<id>.<ext>, for each manifest row"
    echo "  corpus workbooks holding xl/calcChain.xml: $N_CHAIN of $manifest_rows by the survey, $(count_lines "$B/chain-direct") by zipfile (ids: $(paste -sd' ' "$B/chain-ids"))"
    check "the survey's chain count is zipfile's, workbook for workbook" "$(yn cmp -s "$B/chain-ids" "$B/chain-direct")"
    check "some corpus workbook holds a calculation chain, so the chain rows below are read" "$(yn [ "$N_CHAIN" -ge 1 ])"
    printf 'zzzzzzzzzzzz\n' >>"$B/c-chain"
    chain_ctl() { if cmp -s "$B/c-chain" "$B/chain-direct"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: the same comparison tells a planted id list from zipfile's" "$(yn chain_ctl)"
    
    echo
    echo "## the run log's comparison (python3, zipfile, byte spans and ElementTree)"
    # Change BN (part 4a P3's AZ): the comparison is a file beside this script,
    # copied into <work> and printed from there.
    cp "$SELF_DIR/gpcmp.py" "$B/gpcmp.py" || exit 2
    echo "command: cp <scripts>/gpcmp.py <work>/gpcmp.py; sed 's/^/    /' <work>/gpcmp.py; sha256 $(sha_of "$B/gpcmp.py"), $(wc -c <"$B/gpcmp.py") bytes"
    check "the copy is the file beside this script, byte for byte" "$(yn cmp -s "$SELF_DIR/gpcmp.py" "$B/gpcmp.py")"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/gpcmp.py"
    FLAGS="rest_same places schema_order rows_kept rows_window rows_attrs cols_other cols_group cols_bytes format_rest maximums sheetpr_rest outline_pr w_bytes others_same read_back xml_values flagged"
    # flags_of_cmp <comparison>: its FLAGS tuple, read from its source with ast.
    flags_of_cmp() {
      python3 -c 'import ast, sys
    tree = ast.parse(open(sys.argv[1]).read())
    for node in tree.body:
        if isinstance(node, ast.Assign) and getattr(node.targets[0], "id", "") == "FLAGS":
            print(" ".join(e.value for e in node.value.elts))' "$1"
    }
    echo "  the comparison's FLAGS, read from its source: $(flags_of_cmp "$B/gpcmp.py")"
    check "this log's flag list is the comparison's FLAGS" "$(yn [ "$(flags_of_cmp "$B/gpcmp.py")" = "$FLAGS" ])"
    printf 'FLAGS = ("rest_same",)\n' >"$B/c-flags.py"
    check "control: the same reader gives another list for a planted source" "$(yn [ "$(flags_of_cmp "$B/c-flags.py")" = rest_same ])"
    kv() { printf '%s\n' "$1" | tr '\t ' '\n\n' | sed -n "s/^$2=//p" | head -1; }
    all_yes() { local f; for f in $FLAGS; do [ "$(kv "$1" "$f")" = yes ] || return 1; done; }
    # tool_and_cmp <tool line> <comparison line>: the counts the two share
    # (change PC).
    tool_and_cmp() {
      local k
      for k in "rows_before rows_in" "rows_present present" "rows_after rows_out" "cols_before cols_in" "cols_after cols_out" "level_cols level_cols" "kept_cols kept_cols" "r_bound_before r_bound_in"; do
        [ -n "$(kv "$2" "${k#* }")" ] || return 1
        [ "$(kv "$1" "${k% *}")" = "$(kv "$2" "${k#* }")" ] || return 1
      done
    }
    # line_as_spec <tool line>: what "Harness runs" expects of the line (ruling
    # 6): rows_after the rows before plus three less those present, two rows at
    # the level, both hidden, one collapsed, the three flags 1, level_cols 1 or
    # 2, the counts numbers, the relationships prefix 0 or 1 (change PC).
    line_as_spec() {
      local n
      for n in rows_before rows_present rows_after cols_before cols_after kept_cols; do
        case "$(kv "$1" "$n")" in '' | *[!0-9]*) return 1 ;; esac
      done
      [ "$(kv "$1" rows_present)" -le 3 ] || return 1
      [ "$(kv "$1" rows_after)" = "$(( $(kv "$1" rows_before) + 3 - $(kv "$1" rows_present) ))" ] || return 1
      [ "$(kv "$1" level_rows)" = 2 ] && [ "$(kv "$1" hidden_rows)" = 2 ] && [ "$(kv "$1" collapsed_rows)" = 1 ] || return 1
      for n in max_row_ok max_col_ok summary_ok; do
        [ "$(kv "$1" "$n")" = 1 ] || return 1
      done
      case "$(kv "$1" level_cols)" in 1 | 2) ;; *) return 1 ;; esac
      case "$(kv "$1" r_bound_before)" in 0 | 1) return 0 ;; esac
      return 1
    }
    # surveyed_as <tool line> <id>: the line's before-figures are the survey's
    # for the workbook: rows, rows present, cols, the relationships prefix
    # (change PD).
    surveyed_as() {
      [ -n "$(surveyed "$2" 4)" ] || return 1
      [ "$(kv "$1" rows_before)" = "$(surveyed "$2" 4)" ] && [ "$(kv "$1" rows_present)" = "$(surveyed "$2" 5)" ] \
        && [ "$(kv "$1" cols_before)" = "$(surveyed "$2" 6)" ] && [ "$(kv "$1" r_bound_before)" = "$(surveyed "$2" 15)" ]
    }
    ay_ctl() { if all_yes "found=1"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: all_yes refuses a line with no flags" "$(yn ay_ctl)"
    LINE_OK=$(printf 'group\trows_before=20\trows_present=2\trows_after=21\tlevel_rows=2\thidden_rows=2\tcollapsed_rows=1\tcols_before=6\tcols_after=7\tlevel_cols=2\tmax_row_ok=1\tmax_col_ok=1\tsummary_ok=1\tkept_cols=6\tr_bound_before=1')
    lin_ok() { line_as_spec "$LINE_OK"; }
    check "control: line_as_spec accepts a line as the spec reads" "$(yn lin_ok)"
    lin_ctl() { if line_as_spec "$(printf '%s' "$LINE_OK" | sed 's/rows_after=21/rows_after=23/')"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: line_as_spec refuses the same line with three rows created when two were present (ruling 6)" "$(yn lin_ctl)"
    lin_ctl2() { if line_as_spec "$(printf '%s' "$LINE_OK" | sed 's/summary_ok=1/summary_ok=0/')"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: line_as_spec refuses the same line with the summary not set" "$(yn lin_ctl2)"
    CMP_OK="rows_in=20 present=2 rows_out=21 cols_in=6 cols_out=7 level_cols=2 kept_cols=6 r_bound_in=1"
    tac_ok() { tool_and_cmp "$LINE_OK" "$CMP_OK"; }
    check "control: tool_and_cmp accepts a pair that agrees" "$(yn tac_ok)"
    tac_ctl() { if tool_and_cmp "$LINE_OK" "$(printf '%s' "$CMP_OK" | sed 's/cols_out=7/cols_out=8/')"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: tool_and_cmp refuses a pair whose col count disagrees" "$(yn tac_ctl)"
    tac_ctl2() { if tool_and_cmp "$LINE_OK" "$(printf '%s' "$CMP_OK" | sed 's/ r_bound_in=1//')"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: tool_and_cmp refuses a comparison line missing a key" "$(yn tac_ctl2)"
    sa_ctl() { if surveyed_as "$LINE_OK" no-such-id; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: surveyed_as refuses an id the survey has no line for" "$(yn sa_ctl)"
    sa_ok() { local B=$B/c-sa; mkdir -p "$B" && printf 'wb\tx0\t9\t20\t2\t6\t1\t0\t1\tzero\tzero\t2\t0\t0\t1\t0\n' >"$B/survey.out" && surveyed_as "$LINE_OK" x0; }
    check "control: surveyed_as accepts a planted survey line equal to the line's figures" "$(yn sa_ok)"
    sa_ctl2() { local B=$B/c-sa2; mkdir -p "$B" && printf 'wb\tx0\t9\t20\t0\t6\t1\t0\t1\tzero\tzero\t2\t0\t0\t1\t0\n' >"$B/survey.out"; if surveyed_as "$LINE_OK" x0; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: surveyed_as refuses a planted survey line whose rows present differ" "$(yn sa_ctl2)"
    
    count_where() { awk -F'\t' -v c="$2" -v v="$3" 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == c) k = i; next } k && $k == v { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"; }
    # count_ok_where <summary> <column> <value>: among the rows whose outcome is ok.
    count_ok_where() { awk -F'\t' -v c="$2" -v v="$3" 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) { if ($i == c) k = i; if ($i == "outcome") o = i }; next } k && o && $o == "ok" && $k == v { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"; }
    sum_col() { awk -F'\t' -v c="$2" 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == c) k = i; next } k { n += $k } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"; }
    # W's part, and whether the input's entry for it sets general purpose bit 3,
    # for each workbook, read once from the input by the comparison and never
    # printed (changes LC, LF and PC).
    while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do
      python3 "$B/gpcmp.py" "$CORPUS/corpus/$id.$ext" --parts >"$B/parts-$id"
    done <"$B/order"
    # Read by manifest order, never by a glob over parts-*: the controls below
    # write parts-ctl beside them (change JJ).
    n_parts=$(while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do cat "$B/parts-$id"; done <"$B/order" | count_lines /dev/stdin)
    echo "  W's part and its bit 3, read from every input: $n_parts lines"
    check "the comparison found W in every input" "$(yn [ "$n_parts" = "$((2 * manifest_rows))" ])"
    n_bit3=$(while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do sed -n 2p "$B/parts-$id"; done <"$B/order" | count_matches -Fx 1 /dev/stdin)
    n_bit0=$(while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do sed -n 2p "$B/parts-$id"; done <"$B/order" | count_matches -Fx 0 /dev/stdin)
    echo "  input W entries that set bit 3: $n_bit3; do not: $n_bit0; of $manifest_rows"
    check "every input's W entry was read for bit 3 (1 or 0)" "$(yn [ "$((n_bit3 + n_bit0))" = "$manifest_rows" ])"
    # entries_table <entries> <id> <parts file>: the runner's rows for one
    # workbook as changes LC, LF and PC give them: W changed, flagged descriptor
    # exactly when its input entry sets bit 3, else unflagged; every other row
    # identical and unflagged (the calculation chain among them, change PF);
    # nothing added, recompressed or dropped.
    entries_table() {
      local w b
      w=$(sed -n 1p "$3"); b=$(sed -n 2p "$3")
      [ -n "$w" ] && { [ "$b" = 1 ] || [ "$b" = 0 ]; } || return 1
      awk -F'\t' -v id="$2" -v w="$w" -v b="$b" '
        NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) col[$i] = i; next }
        $col["id"] != id { next }
        {
          n++
          nm = $col["name"]
          want = (nm == w) ? "changed" : "identical"
          if ($col["status"] != want) bad++
          wantf = (want == "changed" && b == "1") ? "descriptor" : ""
          if ($col["flags"] != wantf) bad++
          if (want == "changed") nch++
        }
        END { if (n == 0 || bad > 0 || nch != 1) exit 1 }' "$1"
    }
    # want_flagged_of <parts file>: the flagged rows change LF expects, one when
    # W's input entry sets bit 3.
    want_flagged_of() { sed -n 2p "$1" | count_matches -Fx 1 /dev/stdin; }
    # chain_rows_of <entries> <id>: the workbook's calcChain rows, and those
    # identical and unflagged (change PF).
    chain_rows_of() {
      awk -F'\t' -v id="$2" '
        NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) col[$i] = i; next }
        $col["id"] == id && $col["name"] == "xl/calcChain.xml" { n++; if ($col["status"] == "identical" && $col["flags"] == "") s++ }
        END { print n + 0, s + 0 }' "$1"
    }
    printf 'ws.xml\n1\n' >"$B/parts-ctl"
    printf 'ws.xml\n0\n' >"$B/parts-ctl0"
    {
      printf 'id\tname\tstatus\tflags\n'
      printf 'w\t[Content_Types].xml\tidentical\t\nw\tws.xml\tchanged\tdescriptor\nw\txl/calcChain.xml\tidentical\t\nw\tss.xml\tidentical\t\n'
    } >"$B/e-ctl.tsv"
    check "control: entries_table accepts the expected rows of a workbook whose W entry sets bit 3" "$(yn entries_table "$B/e-ctl.tsv" w "$B/parts-ctl")"
    sed 's/ws.xml\tchanged\tdescriptor$/ws.xml\tchanged\t/' "$B/e-ctl.tsv" >"$B/e-ctl0.tsv"
    check "control: entries_table accepts the expected rows of a workbook without bit 3" "$(yn entries_table "$B/e-ctl0.tsv" w "$B/parts-ctl0")"
    sed 's/ss.xml\tidentical\t$/ss.xml\tchanged\t/' "$B/e-ctl.tsv" >"$B/e-extra.tsv"
    en_extra() { if entries_table "$B/e-extra.tsv" w "$B/parts-ctl"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: entries_table refuses another entry changed" "$(yn en_extra)"
    sed 's/ws.xml\tchanged\tdescriptor$/ws.xml\tchanged\trecompressed/' "$B/e-ctl.tsv" >"$B/e-flag.tsv"
    en_flag() { if entries_table "$B/e-flag.tsv" w "$B/parts-ctl"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: entries_table refuses a changed row flagged other than descriptor" "$(yn en_flag)"
    en_nodesc() { if entries_table "$B/e-ctl0.tsv" w "$B/parts-ctl"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: entries_table refuses no flag on a changed row whose input sets bit 3 (change LF)" "$(yn en_nodesc)"
    en_desc() { if entries_table "$B/e-ctl.tsv" w "$B/parts-ctl0"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: entries_table refuses descriptor on a changed row whose input sets no bit 3 (change LF)" "$(yn en_desc)"
    { cat "$B/e-ctl.tsv"; printf 'w\tx.xml\tadded\t\n'; } >"$B/e-add.tsv"
    en_add() { if entries_table "$B/e-add.tsv" w "$B/parts-ctl"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: entries_table refuses an added row" "$(yn en_add)"
    sed 's/ws.xml\tchanged\tdescriptor$/ws.xml\tidentical\t/' "$B/e-ctl.tsv" >"$B/e-same.tsv"
    en_same() { if entries_table "$B/e-same.tsv" w "$B/parts-ctl"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: entries_table refuses rows where W is identical" "$(yn en_same)"
    check "control: want_flagged_of counts the planted bit-3 workbook's one flagged row" "$(yn [ "$(want_flagged_of "$B/parts-ctl")" = 1 ])"
    check "control: want_flagged_of counts none for the planted workbook without bit 3" "$(yn [ "$(want_flagged_of "$B/parts-ctl0")" = 0 ])"
    check "control: chain_rows_of reads the planted workbook's one calcChain row, identical and unflagged" "$(yn [ "$(chain_rows_of "$B/e-ctl.tsv" w)" = "1 1" ])"
    sed 's/calcChain.xml\tidentical\t$/calcChain.xml\tchanged\t/' "$B/e-ctl.tsv" >"$B/e-chain.tsv"
    check "control: chain_rows_of reads a changed calcChain row as not identical" "$(yn [ "$(chain_rows_of "$B/e-chain.tsv" w)" = "1 0" ])"
    # refusal_of <run dir> <id> <label>: the layer's one "error: " line when the
    # row is a refusal (change BK), else nothing.
    refusal_of() { sed -n '1s/^error: //p' "$1/$2/stderr.$3.txt"; }
    
    echo
    echo "## TMPDIR for the corpus runs, on the disk (change LG)"
    RUNTMP=$B/tmp-run
    mkdir "$RUNTMP" || exit 2
    dev_tmp=$(stat -c %d "$RUNTMP")
    dev_corpus=$(stat -c %d "$CORPUS/corpus")
    dev_proc=$(stat -c %d /proc)
    echo "command: mkdir <work>/tmp-run; stat -c %d <work>/tmp-run <corpus>/corpus /proc; df --output=fstype,target <work>/tmp-run <corpus>/corpus"
    echo "  device of TMPDIR (<work>/tmp-run): $dev_tmp; of the corpus directory (<corpus>/corpus): $dev_corpus; of /proc (the control): $dev_proc"
    df --output=fstype,target "$RUNTMP" "$CORPUS/corpus" | sed 's/^/    /'
    check "TMPDIR for the corpus runs and the corpus directory are on one device" "$(yn [ "$dev_tmp" = "$dev_corpus" ])"
    dev_ctl() { if [ "$dev_proc" = "$dev_corpus" ]; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: the same comparison tells /proc's device from the corpus directory's" "$(yn dev_ctl)"
    for label in host i686; do
      var=PT_$label; PT=${!var}; var=XD_$label; XD=${!var}
      echo
      echo "## $label run, --tool-arg $EDIT"
      echo "command: TMPDIR=<work>/tmp-run scripts/passthrough-run.sh --label $label --passthrough <build>/target/$([ "$label" = i686 ] && echo "$I686/")release/emend-copy --xlsx-diff <build>/target/$([ "$label" = i686 ] && echo "$I686/")release/xlsx-diff --out <runs>/$RUN --libreoffice $IMAGE --lo-timeout $LO_TIMEOUT_S --timeout 300 --tool-arg $EDIT"
      started=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)
      TMPDIR=$RUNTMP scripts/passthrough-run.sh --label "$label" --passthrough "$PT" --xlsx-diff "$XD" --out "$OUT" \
        --libreoffice "$IMAGE" --lo-timeout "$LO_TIMEOUT_S" --timeout 300 --tool-arg "$EDIT" \
        >"$B/run-$label.stdout" 2>"$B/run-$label.stderr" </dev/null
      rc=$?
      echo "  started $started; ended $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ); exit $rc; stderr bytes: $(wc -c <"$B/run-$label.stderr")"
      sed 's/^/    /' "$B/run-$label.stdout"
      check "$label: the run exits 0" "$(yn [ "$rc" = 0 ])"
      check "$label: its stderr is empty" "$(yn [ ! -s "$B/run-$label.stderr" ])"
      n_left=$(find "$RUNTMP" -mindepth 1 | wc -l)
      echo "  entries left in <work>/tmp-run after the run: $n_left"
      check "$label: the runs' TMPDIR is empty after the run (change LG)" "$(yn [ "$n_left" = 0 ])"
      SUM=$OUT/summary.$label.tsv
      ENT=$OUT/entries.$label.tsv
      rows=$(awk 'NR > 1' "$SUM" | wc -l)
      n_ok=$(count_where "$SUM" outcome ok)
      # Change BK: the refusals, by id and message.
      : >"$B/refused-$label"
      while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do
        if [ "$(awk -F'\t' -v id="$id" 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) k[$i] = i; next } $k["id"] == id { print $k["outcome"] " " $k["exit"] }' "$SUM")" = "error 2" ] \
           && [ "$(count_lines "$OUT/$id/stderr.$label.txt")" = 1 ] && [ -n "$(refusal_of "$OUT" "$id" "$label")" ]; then
          printf '%s\t%s\n' "$id" "$(refusal_of "$OUT" "$id" "$label")" >>"$B/refused-$label"
        fi
      done <"$B/order"
      n_ref=$(count_lines "$B/refused-$label")
      echo "  summary rows: $rows; outcome ok: $n_ok; refused by the layer (a finding, change BK; fails the summary, change PE): $n_ref"
      sed 's/^/    refused: /' "$B/refused-$label"
      echo "  the refusals by message:"
      cut -f2 "$B/refused-$label" | LC_ALL=C sort | uniq -c | sed 's/^/    /'
      echo "  among the ok rows: lo ok $(count_ok_where "$SUM" lo ok); lo_in ok $(count_ok_where "$SUM" lo_in ok); leftover no $(count_ok_where "$SUM" leftover no); order_preserved yes $(count_ok_where "$SUM" order_preserved yes); comment_equal yes $(count_ok_where "$SUM" comment_equal yes); files_identical no $(count_ok_where "$SUM" files_identical no)"
      echo "  every row: lo_in ok $(count_where "$SUM" lo_in ok); leftover no $(count_where "$SUM" leftover no)"
      echo "  entry totals: identical $(sum_col "$SUM" identical), recompressed $(sum_col "$SUM" recompressed), changed $(sum_col "$SUM" changed), dropped $(sum_col "$SUM" dropped), added $(sum_col "$SUM" added), flagged $(sum_col "$SUM" flagged)"
      summary_ok() {
        local col
        [ "$rows" = "$manifest_rows" ] || return 1
        [ "$n_ok" = "$rows" ] && [ "$n_ref" = 0 ] || return 1
        for col in "lo ok" "lo_in ok" "leftover no" "order_preserved yes" "comment_equal yes" "files_identical no"; do
          [ "$(count_ok_where "$SUM" ${col% *} ${col#* })" = "$n_ok" ] || return 1
        done
        [ "$(count_where "$SUM" lo_in ok)" = "$rows" ] || return 1
        [ "$(count_where "$SUM" leftover no)" = "$rows" ] || return 1
        [ "$(sum_col "$SUM" changed)" = "$want_changed" ] || return 1
        [ "$(sum_col "$SUM" added)" = "$want_added" ] || return 1
        [ "$(sum_col "$SUM" flagged)" = "$want_flagged" ] || return 1
        [ "$(sum_col "$SUM" recompressed)$(sum_col "$SUM" dropped)" = 00 ]
      }
      # The totals the inputs imply over the ok rows: W changed in each,
      # nothing added (change PC), flagged descriptor where its input entry
      # sets bit 3 (change LF).
      want_changed=$n_ok; want_added=0; want_flagged=0
      while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do
        if [ -n "$(awk -F'\t' -v id="$id" '$1 == id' "$B/refused-$label")" ]; then continue; fi
        want_flagged=$((want_flagged + $(want_flagged_of "$B/parts-$id")))
      done <"$B/order"
      echo "  the entry totals the inputs imply: changed $want_changed, added $want_added, flagged $want_flagged"
      check "$label: every row ok (change PE); every row's input opens (lo_in ok) with no leftover; every output opens (lo ok), order and comment kept, files not identical; the changed, added and flagged totals as the inputs imply ($want_changed, $want_added, $want_flagged), none recompressed or dropped" "$(yn summary_ok)"
      echo "  per ok workbook: id, the tool's line, the comparison's line (counts and yes/no only)"
      : >"$B/lines-$label"
      : >"$B/created-$label"
      : >"$B/shapes-$label"
      nwb=0; nflags=0; nagree=0; nline=0; nentries=0; nsurvey=0; io=0; io_want=0; oo=0; oo_want=0; fl=0; fl_want=0
      # Changes PF and PG: the chain rows and the hidden covering columns.
      nchain=0; nchain_same=0; nhidden=0; nhidden_survey=0; nhidden_any=0; npresent=0
      while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do
        if [ -n "$(awk -F'\t' -v id="$id" '$1 == id' "$B/refused-$label")" ]; then continue; fi
        nwb=$((nwb + 1))
        e=$(cat "$OUT/$id/stdout.$label.txt")
        c=$(python3 "$B/gpcmp.py" "$CORPUS/corpus/$id.$ext" "$OUT/$id/out.$label.$ext" --diff "$OUT/$id/diff.$label.tsv")
        printf '%s\t%s\n' "$id" "$e" >>"$B/lines-$label"
        printf '    %s %s\n' "$id" "$(printf '%s' "$e" | tr '\t' ' ')"
        printf '    %s cmp %s\n' "$id" "$(printf '%s' "$c" | tr '\t' ' ')"
        # Change PI: a case is created when its <sheetPr> is.
        printf '%s\t%s\n' "$id" "$(kv "$c" created_sheetpr)" >>"$B/created-$label"
        printf 'created_sheetpr=%s created_format=%s created_cols=%s created_rows=%s edited_rows=%s\n' \
          "$(kv "$c" created_sheetpr)" "$(kv "$c" created_format)" "$(kv "$c" created_cols)" \
          "$(kv "$c" created_rows)" "$(kv "$c" edited_rows)" >>"$B/shapes-$label"
        nhidden=$((nhidden + $(kv "$c" hidden_cols))); nhidden_survey=$((nhidden_survey + $(surveyed "$id" 13)))
        nhidden_any=$((nhidden_any + $(kv "$c" hidden_any_cols)))
        npresent=$((npresent + $(kv "$c" edited_rows)))
        if LC_ALL=C "$G" -qxF "$id" "$B/chain-ids"; then
          cr=$(chain_rows_of "$ENT" "$id")
          nchain=$((nchain + ${cr% *})); nchain_same=$((nchain_same + ${cr#* }))
        fi
        io=$((io + $(kv "$c" in_only))); io_want=$((io_want + $(kv "$c" in_only_want)))
        oo=$((oo + $(kv "$c" out_only))); oo_want=$((oo_want + $(kv "$c" out_only_want)))
        fl=$((fl + $(kv "$c" flagged_rows))); fl_want=$((fl_want + $(kv "$c" flagged_want)))
        if all_yes "$c"; then nflags=$((nflags + 1)); else echo "    $id: a flag of the comparison does not hold"; fi
        if tool_and_cmp "$e" "$c"; then nagree=$((nagree + 1)); else echo "    $id: the tool and the comparison disagree"; fi
        if line_as_spec "$e"; then nline=$((nline + 1)); else echo "    $id: the tool's line is not what the edit implies"; fi
        if surveyed_as "$e" "$id"; then nsurvey=$((nsurvey + 1)); else echo "    $id: the tool's before-figures are not the survey's"; fi
        if entries_table "$ENT" "$id" "$B/parts-$id"; then nentries=$((nentries + 1)); else echo "    $id: the entry rows are not what the sample implies"; fi
      done <"$B/order"
      echo "  ok workbooks read: $nwb; every flag holds: $nflags; the tool and the comparison agree: $nagree; the line as the spec reads: $nline; the before-figures the survey's: $nsurvey; entry rows as P1 expects: $nentries"
      # Change LC: the edit's shapes, counted.
      echo "  the shapes of the edit over the ok workbooks (change PC):"
      LC_ALL=C sort "$B/shapes-$label" | uniq -c | sed 's/^/    /'
      echo "  the xml values rows over the ok workbooks: in_only $io, out_only $oo; the one-sided values the design removes and writes, counted by the comparison: $io_want and $oo_want (change LF)"
      echo "  the flagged entry rows over the ok workbooks: $fl; W entries whose input sets bit 3: $fl_want (change LF)"
      check "$label: the comparison read every ok workbook" "$(yn [ "$nwb" = "$n_ok" ])"
      check "$label: every flag of the comparison holds in every ok workbook" "$(yn [ "$nflags" = "$n_ok" ])"
      check "$label: the tool and the comparison agree in every ok workbook" "$(yn [ "$nagree" = "$n_ok" ])"
      check "$label: every line is what the edits imply" "$(yn [ "$nline" = "$n_ok" ])"
      check "$label: every line's before-figures (rows, rows present, cols) and relationships prefix are the survey's (change PD)" "$(yn [ "$nsurvey" = "$n_ok" ])"
      check "$label: every ok workbook's entry rows are as P1 expects" "$(yn [ "$nentries" = "$n_ok" ])"
      n_shapes=$(count_lines "$B/shapes-$label")
      check "$label: one shape counted per ok workbook ($n_shapes)" "$(yn [ "$n_shapes" = "$n_ok" ])"
      vals_ok() { [ "$io" = "$io_want" ] && [ "$oo" = "$oo_want" ] && [ "$oo" -ge 1 ]; }
      check "$label: the in_only and out_only totals are the derived totals, and some value was written (change LF)" "$(yn vals_ok)"
      fl_ok() { [ "$fl" = "$fl_want" ] && [ "$fl" = "$(sum_col "$SUM" flagged)" ]; }
      check "$label: the flagged total is the derived total and the summary's (change LF)" "$(yn fl_ok)"
      echo "  rows numbered M + 1 to M + 3 edited in place over the ok workbooks (ruling 6): $npresent; the survey's: $SV_PRESENT"
      check "$label: the rows edited in place are the survey's present rows (ruling 6)" "$(yn [ "$npresent" = "$SV_PRESENT" ])"
      echo "  <col> elements covering column 2 or 3 with hidden=\"1\", which the group removed (ruling 3): $nhidden; the survey's: $nhidden_survey"
      check "$label: the hidden covering columns the comparison counted are the survey's (ruling 3)" "$(yn [ "$nhidden" = "$nhidden_survey" ])"
      echo "  <col> elements covering column 2 or 3 with a hidden attribute of any value, which the group dropped: $nhidden_any; the survey's: $SV_HIDDEN_ANY"
      check "$label: the covering columns with any hidden attribute the comparison counted are the survey's" "$(yn [ "$nhidden_any" = "$SV_HIDDEN_ANY" ])"
      echo "  calcChain rows in the ok rows of the chain workbooks: $nchain; identical and unflagged: $nchain_same (change PF)"
      chain_kept() { [ "$nchain" = "$N_CHAIN" ] && [ "$nchain_same" = "$nchain" ]; }
      check "$label: every chain workbook has one calcChain row, identical and unflagged (change PF)" "$(yn chain_kept)"
      R=$OUT/run.$label.tsv
      args=$(awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == "tool_args") k = i; next } k && NR == 2 { print $k }' "$R")
      bins_in_row() { [ "$(awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) k[$i] = i; next } NR == 2 { print $k["passthrough_sha256"] " " $k["xlsx_diff_sha256"] " " $k["commit"] }' "$R")" = "$(sha_of "$PT") $(sha_of "$XD") $C" ]; }
      check "$label: the run row records the two release binaries by sha256 and the phase commit" "$(yn bins_in_row)"
      check "$label: the run row's tool_args is $EDIT" "$(yn [ "$args" = "$EDIT" ])"
    done
    check "the same workbooks are refused on both targets, with the same messages (none, change PE)" "$(yn cmp -s "$B/refused-host" "$B/refused-i686")"
    echo "the calc chain: $N_CHAIN of the corpus's $manifest_rows workbooks hold xl/calcChain.xml; on each label each of their calcChain entries is identical and unflagged, by the entries rule (every entry but W identical and unflagged; no formula changes, so the formula-change rule does not fire), which keeps the chain"
    printf 'x\tsome message\n' >"$B/c-refused"
    ref_ctl() { if cmp -s "$B/c-refused" "$B/refused-host"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: the same comparison tells a planted refusal list from the host's" "$(yn ref_ctl)"
    mkdir -p "$B/c-refrun/r1"
    printf 'error: a planted message\n' >"$B/c-refrun/r1/stderr.host.txt"
    ref_read() { [ "$(refusal_of "$B/c-refrun" r1 host)" = "a planted message" ]; }
    check "control: refusal_of reads a planted refusal's message" "$(yn ref_read)"
    : >"$B/c-refrun/r1/stderr.host.txt"
    ref_none() { [ -z "$(refusal_of "$B/c-refrun" r1 host)" ]; }
    check "control: refusal_of reads nothing from an empty standard error" "$(yn ref_none)"
    entries_ctl() {
      local id
      id=$(head -n 1 "$B/order" | cut -f1)
      printf 'no/such/part.xml\n0\n' >"$B/c-parts"
      if entries_table "$OUT/entries.host.tsv" "$id" "$B/c-parts"; then return 1; else return 0; fi
    }
    check "control: entries_table refuses the first workbook's rows against parts it does not change" "$(yn entries_ctl)"
    
    echo
    echo "### the planted-flag controls, host, each on the first ok workbook in manifest order whose <sheetPr> is created and on the first whose <sheetPr> is kept (change PI)"
    first_case() { awk -F'\t' -v v="$1" '$2 == v { print $1; exit }' "$B/created-host"; }
    CASE_CREATED=$(first_case 1)
    CASE_KEPT=$(first_case 0)
    echo "  the created case: ${CASE_CREATED:-none}; the kept case: ${CASE_KEPT:-none}"
    both_cases() { [ -n "$CASE_CREATED" ] && [ -n "$CASE_KEPT" ]; }
    check "the corpus gives a created case and a kept case" "$(yn both_cases)"
    nplants=0; nbit_c=0; nbit_k=0
    for f in $FLAGS; do
      nplants=$((nplants + 1))
      for case in created kept; do
        if [ "$case" = created ]; then id=$CASE_CREATED; else id=$CASE_KEPT; fi
        planted=""
        if [ -n "$id" ]; then
          ext=$(awk -F'\t' -v id="$id" '$1 == id { print $2 }' "$B/order")
          planted=$(python3 "$B/gpcmp.py" "$CORPUS/corpus/$id.$ext" "$OUT/$id/out.host.$ext" --diff "$OUT/$id/diff.host.tsv" --plant "$f")
        fi
        flag=$f
        turned() { [ -n "$planted" ] && [ "$(kv "$planted" "$flag")" = no ] && [ "$(kv "$planted" planted)" = yes ]; }
        echo "  plant $f on the $case case ${id:-none}: planted=$(kv "$planted" planted); $flag=$(kv "$planted" "$flag")"
        if turned; then
          if [ "$case" = created ]; then nbit_c=$((nbit_c + 1)); else nbit_k=$((nbit_k + 1)); fi
        fi
        check "control: the plant $f on the $case case turns $flag to no" "$(yn turned)"
      done
    done
    echo "  plants per case: $nplants; that turned their own flag: created $nbit_c, kept $nbit_k"
    check "every flag has a plant that turned it on the created case ($nbit_c of $nplants)" "$(yn [ "$nbit_c" = "$nplants" ])"
    check "every flag has a plant that turned it on the kept case ($nbit_k of $nplants)" "$(yn [ "$nbit_k" = "$nplants" ])"
    first_ok=$(head -n 1 "$B/lines-host" | cut -f1)
    first_ext=$(awk -F'\t' -v id="$first_ok" '$1 == id { print $2 }' "$B/order")
    unknown_plant() { [ "$(python3 "$B/gpcmp.py" "$CORPUS/corpus/$first_ok.$first_ext" "$OUT/$first_ok/out.host.$first_ext" --plant no_such_flag)" = error=unknown-plant ]; }
    check "control: the comparison refuses a plant it does not know" "$(yn unknown_plant)"
    
    echo
    echo "### the two labels' outputs"
    same_out=0
    nboth=0
    while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do
      if [ -n "$(awk -F'\t' -v id="$id" '$1 == id' "$B/refused-host")" ]; then continue; fi
      nboth=$((nboth + 1))
      if cmp -s "$OUT/$id/out.host.$ext" "$OUT/$id/out.i686.$ext"; then same_out=$((same_out + 1)); else echo "    $id: the outputs differ"; fi
    done <"$B/order"
    echo "  ok workbooks: $nboth; whose host and i686 outputs are byte for byte the same: $same_out"
    check "every output is the same on both targets" "$(yn [ "$same_out" = "$nboth" ])"
    check "both targets printed the same line for every ok workbook" "$(yn cmp -s "$B/lines-host" "$B/lines-i686")"
    cp "$B/lines-host" "$B/c-lines"; printf 'x\n' >>"$B/c-lines"
    lines_ctl() { if cmp -s "$B/c-lines" "$B/lines-i686"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: the same comparison tells a line list with one line added" "$(yn lines_ctl)"
    
    echo
    echo "## the corpus record pair"
    echo "command: scripts/passthrough-record.py --run <runs>/$RUN --out <scripts>/out/records --stem $STEM_RUN"
    scripts/passthrough-record.py --run "$OUT" --out "$RECORDS" --stem "$STEM_RUN" >"$B/record.out" 2>&1
    rrc=$?
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/record.out"
    check "the record script exits 0" "$(yn [ "$rrc" = 0 ])"
    cat >"$B/reccheck.py" <<'PY'
    """This log's check of a passthrough record against its run directory, for
    every label the directory holds. Reads the record's .txt and .md and the run
    directory's summary.<label>.tsv, entries.<label>.tsv and each workbook's
    diff.<label>.tsv; prints one "name: yes|no" line per check and one line of
    counts. It imports only the part-family rules from
    scripts/passthrough-record.py, so the check covers the record's tables and
    its counting, not the family names."""
    import importlib.util
    import os
    import sys
    
    sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
    rec_script, run_dir, txt, md, want_changed, want_added, tool_arg = sys.argv[1:8]
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("record", rec_script)
    record = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    spec.loader.exec_module(record)
    
    
    def lines(path):
        out = open(path, encoding="utf-8").read().split("\n")
        return out[:-1] if out and out[-1] == "" else out
    
    
    labels = [l for l in ("host", "i686") if os.path.exists("%s/summary.%s.tsv" % (run_dir, l))]
    tables = "\n".join(lines(txt)).split("\n\n")
    summary, entries, xml = [], [], ["\t".join(record.XML_HEADER)]
    per_label = {}
    for label in labels:
        s = lines("%s/summary.%s.tsv" % (run_dir, label))
        e = lines("%s/entries.%s.tsv" % (run_dir, label))
        summary = summary or [s[0]]
        entries = entries or [e[0]]
        summary += s[1:]
        entries += e[1:]
        x = []
        for row in s[1:]:
            cells = dict(zip(s[0].split("\t"), row.split("\t")))
            if cells["outcome"] != "ok" or cells["diff_exit"] not in ("0", "1"):
                continue
            for line in lines("%s/%s/diff.%s.tsv" % (run_dir, cells["id"], label)):
                c = line.split("\t")
                if c[0] == "xml":
                    x.append("\t".join([cells["id"], label] + c + [""] * (10 - 2 - len(c))))
        xml += x
        per_label[label] = (e, x)
    checks = [
        ("three tables", len(tables) == 3),
        ("the summary table is every label's summary", len(tables) == 3 and tables[0].split("\n") == summary),
        ("the entries table is every label's entries", len(tables) == 3 and tables[1].split("\n") == entries),
        ("the xml table is every compared workbook's xml rows", len(tables) == 3 and tables[2].split("\n") == xml),
    ]
    text = lines(md)
    
    
    def section(title):
        out, on = [], False
        for line in text:
            if line == "## " + title:
                on = True
                continue
            if on and line.startswith("## "):
                break
            if on and line.startswith("| ") and not line.startswith("| ---"):
                out.append(line)
        return out[1:]
    
    
    def row(cells):
        return "| " + " | ".join(str(c) for c in cells) + " |"
    
    
    cols = ("entries",) + record.STATUSES + ("flagged",) + record.FLAGS
    xcols = ("compared", "parse_errors", "names_equal", "values_equal", "in_only", "out_only")
    for label in labels:
        e, x = per_label[label]
        head = e[0].split("\t")
        fam = {}
        for line in e[1:]:
            r = dict(zip(head, line.split("\t")))
            c = fam.setdefault(record.family(r["name"]), dict.fromkeys(cols, 0))
            c["entries"] += 1
            c[r["status"]] = c.get(r["status"], 0) + 1
            flags = [f for f in r["flags"].split(",") if f]
            c["flagged"] += 1 if flags else 0
            for f in flags:
                c[f] = c.get(f, 0) + 1
        want = [row([f] + [fam[f][k] for k in cols]) for f in record.FAMILIES if f in fam]
        want.append(row(["total"] + [sum(fam[f][k] for f in fam) for k in cols]))
        checks.append(("%s: each family row of Entries by part family" % label, section("Entries by part family: " + label) == want))
        xf, cur = {}, None
        for line in x:
            c = line.split("\t")
            name, kind = c[3], c[4]
            if kind == "parse":
                cur = xf.setdefault(record.family(name), dict.fromkeys(xcols, 0))
                cur["compared"] += 1
                parsed = c[5] == "ok" and c[6] == "ok"
                cur["parse_errors"] += 0 if parsed else 1
                differ = False
            elif kind in ("element", "attribute"):
                differ = True
            elif kind == "values":
                cur["names_equal"] += 1 if parsed and not differ else 0
                cur["values_equal"] += 1 if c[7] == "0" and c[8] == "0" else 0
                cur["in_only"] += int(c[7])
                cur["out_only"] += int(c[8])
        want = [row([f] + [xf[f][k] for k in xcols]) for f in record.FAMILIES if f in xf]
        want.append(row(["total"] + [sum(xf[f][k] for f in xf) for k in xcols]))
        checks.append(("%s: each family row of the XML comparison" % label, section("XML comparison of changed entries: " + label) == want))
        changed_f = sorted(f for f in fam if fam[f].get("changed"))
        dropped_f = sorted(f for f in fam if fam[f].get("dropped"))
        added_f = sorted(f for f in fam if fam[f].get("added"))
        # Change CD: the families the --parts lines imply, changed and added;
        # nothing dropped.
        checks.append(("%s: the xml families are the changed entries' families" % label, sorted(xf) == changed_f))
        checks.append(("%s: the changed entries' families are %s" % (label, want_changed), changed_f == want_changed.split(",")))
        checks.append(("%s: no entry is dropped" % label, dropped_f == []))
        # Change JC: no family added is the empty list, not a list of one empty
        # name.
        checks.append(("%s: the added entries' families are %s" % (label, want_added or "none"), added_f == (want_added.split(",") if want_added else [])))
    checks.append(("the record's Targets line", "- Targets: " + ", ".join(labels) in text))
    checks.append(("the record's Tool arguments line", "- Tool arguments: " + tool_arg in text))
    for name, ok in checks:
        print("%s: %s" % (name, "yes" if ok else "no"))
    print("labels %s; summary rows %d; entry rows %d; xml rows %d" % (",".join(labels), len(summary) - 1, len(entries) - 1, len(xml) - 1))
    PY
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/reccheck.py"
    RTXT=$RECORDS/$STEM_RUN.txt
    RMD=$RECORDS/$STEM_RUN.md
    # The families the --parts lines imply (change JC), over every input: W's,
    # by the record script's own family rule, changed; nothing added.
    while IFS="$TAB" read -r id ext; do sed -n 1p "$B/parts-$id"; done <"$B/order" >"$B/w.parts"
    check "W's part read for every manifest row, by manifest order ($(count_lines "$B/w.parts"))" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$B/w.parts")" = "$manifest_rows" ])"
    FAM_CHANGED=$(python3 -c 'import importlib.util, sys
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("record", sys.argv[1])
    record = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    spec.loader.exec_module(record)
    print(",".join(sorted({record.family(l) for l in open(sys.argv[2]).read().split() if l})))' scripts/passthrough-record.py "$B/w.parts")
    FAM_ADDED=
    echo "  the families the inputs imply: changed $FAM_CHANGED; added ${FAM_ADDED:-none}"
    check "the changed families were derived (some family)" "$(yn [ -n "$FAM_CHANGED" ])"
    python3 "$B/reccheck.py" scripts/passthrough-record.py "$OUT" "$RTXT" "$RMD" "$FAM_CHANGED" "$FAM_ADDED" "$EDIT" >"$B/reccheck.out" 2>&1
    echo "  exit: $?"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/reccheck.out"
    rec_all() { [ "$(count_matches -E ': yes$' "$B/reccheck.out")" = 18 ] && [ "$(count_matches -E ': no$' "$B/reccheck.out")" = 0 ]; }
    check "the record's three tables are the run directory's, and its family tables are counted from them (eighteen checks: four, six per label, two)" "$(yn rec_all)"
    awk '!done && /^[|] total [|]/ { done = 1; next } { print }' "$RMD" >"$B/c-rec.md"
    python3 "$B/reccheck.py" scripts/passthrough-record.py "$OUT" "$RTXT" "$B/c-rec.md" "$FAM_CHANGED" "$FAM_ADDED" "$EDIT" >"$B/c-reccheck.out" 2>&1
    sed '2d' "$RTXT" >"$B/c-rec.txt"
    python3 "$B/reccheck.py" scripts/passthrough-record.py "$OUT" "$B/c-rec.txt" "$RMD" "$FAM_CHANGED" "$FAM_ADDED" "$EDIT" >"$B/c-reccheck2.out" 2>&1
    rec_ctl() { [ "$(count_matches -E ': no$' "$B/c-reccheck.out")" -ge 1 ] && [ "$(count_matches -F "the summary table is every label's summary: no" "$B/c-reccheck2.out")" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same check finds an .md with a family table's total row dropped and a .txt one summary row short" "$(yn rec_ctl)"
    # Change JI: no bytecode was written, so there is nothing to remove.
    no_pycache() { [ ! -e scripts/__pycache__ ]; }
    check "the record script and the record check left no scripts/__pycache__ (PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE)" "$(yn no_pycache)"
    echo "command: install -m 644 <scripts>/out/records/$STEM_RUN.md <scripts>/out/records/$STEM_RUN.txt <repo>/$RECORDS_DEST/"
    install -m 644 "$RMD" "$RTXT" "$RECORDS_DEST"/ && INSTALLED+=("$RECORDS_DEST/$STEM_RUN.md" "$RECORDS_DEST/$STEM_RUN.txt")
    echo "  exit: $?"
    for f in "$STEM_RUN.md" "$STEM_RUN.txt"; do
      echo "    installed $RECORDS_DEST/$f: sha256 $(sha_of "$RECORDS_DEST/$f"), $(wc -c <"$RECORDS_DEST/$f") bytes, mode $(stat -c %a "$RECORDS_DEST/$f")"
      inst_same() { cmp -s "$RECORDS/$1" "$RECORDS_DEST/$1" && [ "$(stat -c %a "$RECORDS_DEST/$1")" = 644 ]; }
      check "the installed $f is the written one, mode 644" "$(yn inst_same "$f")"
    done
    echo
    if [ "$RUN_SKIP_KEEP" = yes ]; then
    echo "## the keep and the open check: SKIPPED (RUN_SKIP_KEEP=yes, a dry run; change JE)"
    else
    echo "## the keep regenerated: the tests with the variable set, one keep directory per target"
    echo "command: read the test.log given (sha256 $(sha_of "$TEST_LOG"), $(wc -c <"$TEST_LOG") bytes)"
    tl_is_phase() { [ "$(count_matches -E "^about: M3 part 4 P1 phase commit $C; HEAD at run: $C\$" "$TEST_LOG")" = 1 ]; }
    check "the test.log read is this phase's, at this phase commit" "$(yn tl_is_phase)"
    tl_ctl() { local C=$NULL_SHA; if tl_is_phase; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: the same check says no for the null commit" "$(yn tl_ctl)"
    tl_unset() { [ "$(count_matches -xF 'EMEND_KEEP_DIR set when this script started: no; unset for the whole log: yes' "$TEST_LOG")" = 1 ]; }
    check "the test.log ran with the variable unset" "$(yn tl_unset)"
    tl_all_yes() { [ "$(count_matches -xF 'test log checks all as expected: yes' "$TEST_LOG")" = 1 ]; }
    check "the test.log ends all as expected" "$(yn tl_all_yes)"
    for target in host i686-unknown-linux-musl; do
      awk -v h="## cargo test --workspace ($target)" '
        $0 == h { on = 1; next }
        /^## / { on = 0 }
        on && /^    test .* \.\.\. ok$/ { sub(/^    test /, ""); sub(/ \.\.\. ok$/, ""); print }
      ' "$TEST_LOG" | sort >"$B/unset-$target.names"
      sed -n "s/^$target: passed \\([0-9]*\\); failed 0; ignored \\([0-9]*\\); test lines ending ok: [0-9]*\$/\\1 \\2/p" "$TEST_LOG" >"$B/unset-$target.count"
      echo "  $target without the variable: passed and ignored $(cat "$B/unset-$target.count"); names read $(count_lines "$B/unset-$target.names")"
      names_match_count() { [ -s "$B/unset-$target.count" ] && [ "$(count_lines "$B/unset-$target.names")" = "$(cut -d' ' -f1 "$B/unset-$target.count")" ]; }
      check "$target: the names read account for the passed count read" "$(yn names_match_count)"
    done
    mkdir "$KEEP" "$BUILD_ROOT/keep-i686.$$" || exit 2
    KI=$BUILD_ROOT/keep-i686.$$
    for target in host i686-unknown-linux-musl; do
      case $target in host) K=$KEEP; targs=() ;; *) K=$KI; targs=(--target "$target") ;; esac
      echo
      echo "### cargo test --workspace ($target), EMEND_KEEP_DIR=$K"
      echo "command: EMEND_KEEP_DIR=$K cargo test --workspace ${targs[*]}"
      EMEND_KEEP_DIR=$K cargo test --workspace "${targs[@]}" >"$B/$target.out" 2>&1 </dev/null
      rc=$?
      echo "  exit: $rc"
      check "$target: exit 0" "$(yn [ "$rc" -eq 0 ])"
      echo "  summary lines:"
      LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^ *Running |^ *Doc-tests |^test result: ' "$B/$target.out" | sed 's/^ */    /'
      LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^test .* \.\.\. ok$' "$B/$target.out" | sed -E 's/^test (.*) \.\.\. ok$/\1/' | sort >"$B/set-$target.names"
      passed=$(awk '/^test result: / { for (i = 1; i < NF; i++) if ($(i + 1) ~ /^passed;$/) n += $i } END { print n + 0 }' "$B/$target.out")
      failed=$(awk '/^test result: / { for (i = 1; i < NF; i++) if ($(i + 1) ~ /^failed;$/) n += $i } END { print n + 0 }' "$B/$target.out")
      ignored=$(awk '/^test result: / { for (i = 1; i < NF; i++) if ($(i + 1) ~ /^ignored;$/) n += $i } END { print n + 0 }' "$B/$target.out")
      echo "  $target with the variable: passed $passed; failed $failed; ignored $ignored; test lines ending ok $(count_lines "$B/set-$target.names")"
      check "$target: failed is 0" "$(yn [ "$failed" = 0 ])"
      check "$target: passed and ignored are the run's without the variable ($(cat "$B/unset-$target.count"))" "$(yn [ "$passed $ignored" = "$(cat "$B/unset-$target.count")" ])"
      check "$target: the test names that passed are the run's without the variable" "$(yn cmp -s "$B/set-$target.names" "$B/unset-$target.names")"
      echo "  files in the keep: $(find "$K" -type f | wc -l); entries that are not regular files: $(find "$K" -mindepth 1 ! -type f | wc -l)"
    done
    { head -n 1 "$B/unset-host.names"; cat "$B/unset-host.names"; } | sort >"$B/c-names"
    cmp_ctl() { if cmp -s "$B/c-names" "$B/unset-host.names"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: the same comparison tells a name list with one name doubled from the real one" "$(yn cmp_ctl)"
    
    echo
    echo "## the two keep directories compared"
    (cd "$KEEP" && find . -mindepth 1 -printf '%P\n' | LC_ALL=C sort) >"$B/host.files"
    (cd "$KI" && find . -mindepth 1 -printf '%P\n' | LC_ALL=C sort) >"$B/i686.files"
    nfiles=$(count_lines "$B/host.files")
    same=0
    while IFS= read -r f; do
      if cmp -s "$KEEP/$f" "$KI/$f"; then same=$((same + 1)); else echo "    differs: $f"; fi
    done <"$B/host.files"
    echo "  files: host $nfiles, i686 $(count_lines "$B/i686.files"); the same bytes on both: $same"
    check "the two keeps hold the same names" "$(yn cmp -s "$B/host.files" "$B/i686.files")"
    keeps_same() { [ "$nfiles" -ge 2 ] && [ "$same" = "$nfiles" ]; }
    check "every file in the host keep is byte for byte the i686 keep's" "$(yn keeps_same)"
    first_kept=$(head -n 1 "$B/host.files")
    cp "$KEEP/$first_kept" "$B/c-copy"
    printf 'x' >>"$B/c-copy"
    cmp_bytes_ctl() { if cmp -s "$B/c-copy" "$KI/$first_kept"; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: cmp tells a kept file with one byte added from its original" "$(yn cmp_bytes_ctl)"
    n_in=$(count_matches -E '\.in\.xlsx$' "$B/host.files")
    n_out=$(count_matches -E '\.out\.xlsx$' "$B/host.files")
    n_other=$(count_matches -vE '^[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+\.[0-9]+\.(in|out)\.xlsx$' "$B/host.files")
    LC_ALL=C sed -nE 's/^(.*)\.in\.xlsx$/\1/p' "$B/host.files" | LC_ALL=C sort >"$B/pair.names"
    LC_ALL=C sed -nE 's/^(.*)\.out\.xlsx$/\1/p' "$B/host.files" | LC_ALL=C sort >"$B/pair.out.names"
    echo "  .in.xlsx $n_in; .out.xlsx $n_out; names not of the form <test>.<n>.in|out.xlsx: $n_other"
    all_pairs() { [ "$n_in" = "$n_out" ] && [ "$((n_in * 2))" = "$nfiles" ] && [ "$n_other" = 0 ] && cmp -s "$B/pair.names" "$B/pair.out.names"; }
    check "the keep holds only whole pairs named <test>.<n>" "$(yn all_pairs)"
    NPAIRS=$n_in
    (cd "$KEEP" && find . -type f -printf '%P\t%s\n' | LC_ALL=C sort) >"$B/keep.listing"
    echo "  the host keep's listing: pairs $(count_matches -E "[.]in[.]xlsx${TAB}" "$B/keep.listing"); files $(count_lines "$B/keep.listing"); listing sha256 $(sha_of "$B/keep.listing")"
    check "the host keep's pairs times two equals its files (keep_pairs_ok)" "$(yn keep_pairs_ok "$B/keep.listing")"
    # Change JI: the i686 keep is kept, not removed.
    check "the i686 keep stays beside the host keep under <build>, not removed (change JI)" "$(yn [ -d "$KI" ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## the host keep against M3 part 3 P4's committed open-check record, named by its record commit (changes AU, BP, BR, BW, CC, JB, LB, MB, NB and PB)"
    PREV_TXT=$(git show --name-only --format= "$PREV_OPEN_REC" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^records/m3p3-open-.*[.]txt$')
    echo "command: git show --name-only --format= $PREV_OPEN_REC, the open-check .txt it added; git show <phase commit>:<it>"
    echo "  M3 part 3 P4's record: $PREV_TXT (sha256 $(git show "$C:$PREV_TXT" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1))"
    check "M3 part 3 P4's record commit added exactly one open-check .txt" "$(yn [ "$(printf '%s\n' "$PREV_TXT" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 1 ])"
    no_later_open() { [ -z "$(git log --format=%H "$PREV_OPEN_REC..$C" -- 'records/*-open-*.txt')" ]; }
    check "no commit after it adds an open-check record, so it is the last committed" "$(yn no_later_open)"
    git show "$C:$PREV_TXT" >"$B/prev.txt"
    while IFS= read -r t; do
      printf '%s\t%s\t%s\t%s\t%s\n' "$t" "$(stat -c %s "$KEEP/$t.in.xlsx")" "$(sha_of "$KEEP/$t.in.xlsx")" \
        "$(stat -c %s "$KEEP/$t.out.xlsx")" "$(sha_of "$KEEP/$t.out.xlsx")"
    done <"$B/pair.names" >"$B/keep.rows"
    tail -n +2 "$B/prev.txt" | cut -f1-5 | LC_ALL=C sort >"$B/prev.rows"
    LC_ALL=C sort "$B/keep.rows" >"$B/keep.sorted"
    n_prev=$(count_lines "$B/prev.rows")
    n_kept_prev=$(LC_ALL=C comm -12 "$B/prev.rows" "$B/keep.sorted" | count_lines /dev/stdin)
    cut -f1 "$B/prev.rows" >"$B/prev.names"
    LC_ALL=C comm -13 "$B/prev.names" <(cut -f1 "$B/keep.sorted") >"$B/new.pairs"
    LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$B/prev.names" <(cut -f1 "$B/keep.sorted") >"$B/gone.pairs"
    echo "  rows: the regenerated keep $(count_lines "$B/keep.rows"), M3 part 3 P4's record $n_prev; its rows found in the keep with the same name, bytes and both sha256s: $n_kept_prev"
    echo "  pairs in the keep and not in M3 part 3 P4's record: $(count_lines "$B/new.pairs"); in its record and not in the keep: $(count_lines "$B/gone.pairs")"
    sed 's/^/    new: /' "$B/new.pairs"
    LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$B/prev.rows" "$B/keep.sorted" | cut -f1 >"$B/changed.pairs"
    echo "  pairs of M3 part 3 P4's record whose bytes differ in the keep: $(count_lines "$B/changed.pairs")"
    sed 's/^/    changed: /' "$B/changed.pairs"
    check "no pair of M3 part 3 P4's record is gone" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$B/gone.pairs")" = 0 ])"
    check "every pair of M3 part 3 P4's record is in the keep, unchanged or changed ($n_kept_prev + $(count_lines "$B/changed.pairs") = $n_prev)" "$(yn [ "$((n_kept_prev + $(count_lines "$B/changed.pairs")))" = "$n_prev" ])"
    echo "command: the #[test] functions added or whose body is edited since the named record commit, from the two commits' sources of every .rs file git diff --name-only <named record commit> <phase commit> names: <work>/edited.py, below"
    cat >"$B/edited.py" <<'PY'
    """The #[test] functions whose body differs between two commits, or that
    the second adds: each file's text at both commits (git show), every
    function after a #[test] attribute (other attributes allowed between), its
    body from the fn line to the first line that is a lone closing brace in
    column one. Prints one test name per line."""
    import re
    import subprocess
    import sys
    
    base, head = sys.argv[1:3]
    TEST = re.compile(r"#\[test\]\s*(?:#\[[^\]]*\]\s*)*fn\s+([A-Za-z0-9_]+)")
    
    
    def show(rev, path):
        run = subprocess.run(["git", "show", "%s:%s" % (rev, path)], capture_output=True)
        return run.stdout.decode() if run.returncode == 0 else ""
    
    
    def tests(text):
        out = {}
        for m in TEST.finditer(text):
            end = text.find("\n}\n", m.start())
            out[m.group(1)] = text[m.start():end if end >= 0 else len(text)]
        return out
    
    
    names = subprocess.run(["git", "diff", "--name-only", base, head, "--", "*.rs"],
                           capture_output=True, check=True).stdout.decode().split()
    edited = set()
    for path in names:
        before, after = tests(show(base, path)), tests(show(head, path))
        for name, body in after.items():
            if before.get(name) != body:
                edited.add(name)
    for name in sorted(edited):
        print(name)
    PY
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/edited.py"
    # Change JF (M3 part 1 P3's IC): from the named record commit, since the
    # record compared with is its.
    python3 "$B/edited.py" "$PREV_OPEN_REC" "$C" | LC_ALL=C sort >"$B/edited.tests"
    sed 's/^/    added or edited test: /' "$B/edited.tests"
    sed -E 's/\.[0-9]+$//; s/^.*\.//' "$B/new.pairs" | LC_ALL=C sort -u >"$B/new.tests"
    sed -E 's/\.[0-9]+$//; s/^.*\.//' "$B/changed.pairs" | LC_ALL=C sort -u >"$B/changed.tests"
    echo "  tests with a new pair: $(count_lines "$B/new.tests"); tests with a changed pair: $(count_lines "$B/changed.tests"); tests added or edited: $(count_lines "$B/edited.tests")"
    check "some test is added or edited, so the list was read" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$B/edited.tests")" -ge 1 ])"
    new_from_edited() { [ "$(LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$B/new.tests" "$B/edited.tests" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 0 ]; }
    check "every new pair is kept by a test this phase adds or edits" "$(yn new_from_edited)"
    changed_from_edited() { [ "$(LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$B/changed.tests" "$B/edited.tests" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 0 ]; }
    check "every changed pair of M3 part 3 P4's record is kept by a test this phase edits (the code under the other tests did not change what they write)" "$(yn changed_from_edited)"
    printf 'zzz_not_an_edited_test\n' | LC_ALL=C sort -m - "$B/new.tests" >"$B/c-new.tests"
    new_ctl() { [ "$(LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$B/c-new.tests" "$B/edited.tests" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same comparison finds a pair of a test the phase did not add or edit" "$(yn new_ctl)"
    
    echo
    echo "## scripts/edit-open-check.sh on the host keep (specs/0018 \"Harness runs\": every phase's run log runs it over its keep)"
    mkdir "$B/tmp"
    # Change MF (specs/0025 P1 verification ruling 3, L2): the open check's own
    # TMPDIR, its device beside the runs' and the corpus directory's.
    dev_open=$(stat -c %d "$B/tmp")
    echo "command: stat -c %d <work>/tmp <work>/tmp-run <corpus>/corpus /proc"
    echo "  device of the open check's TMPDIR (<work>/tmp): $dev_open; of the runs' TMPDIR (<work>/tmp-run): $(stat -c %d "$RUNTMP"); of the corpus directory (<corpus>/corpus): $dev_corpus; of /proc (the control): $dev_proc"
    check "the open check's TMPDIR and the corpus directory are on one device (change MF)" "$(yn [ "$dev_open" = "$dev_corpus" ])"
    dev_open_ctl() { if [ "$dev_proc" = "$dev_open" ]; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: the same comparison tells /proc's device from the open check's TMPDIR's" "$(yn dev_open_ctl)"
    echo "command: TMPDIR=<work>/tmp scripts/edit-open-check.sh --keep <keep> --libreoffice $IMAGE --out <scripts>/out/records --stem $STEM_OPEN"
    TMPDIR=$B/tmp scripts/edit-open-check.sh --keep "$KEEP" --libreoffice "$IMAGE" --out "$RECORDS" --stem "$STEM_OPEN" \
      >"$B/oc.stdout" 2>"$B/oc.stderr" </dev/null
    oc_rc=$?
    echo "  exit: $oc_rc"
    echo "  stdout:"; sed 's/^/    /' "$B/oc.stdout"
    echo "  stderr bytes: $(wc -c <"$B/oc.stderr")"
    check "the script exits 0 (no finding, no check errored)" "$(yn [ "$oc_rc" = 0 ])"
    check "its stderr is empty" "$(yn [ ! -s "$B/oc.stderr" ])"
    echo "  the reasons the script kept (its reasons directory under <work>/tmp), one line per refused side:"
    find "$B/tmp" -name '*-reason.txt' | LC_ALL=C sort | while IFS= read -r f; do echo "    ${f#"$B/tmp/"}: $(cat "$f")"; done
    TXT=$RECORDS/$STEM_OPEN.txt
    MD=$RECORDS/$STEM_OPEN.md
    TXT_HEADER=$(git show "$C:scripts/edit-open-check.sh" | sed -n "s/^readonly TXT_HEADER=\\$'\\(.*\\)'\$/\\1/p" | sed 's/\\t/\t/g')
    check "the .txt's header is the script's TXT_HEADER, read from the phase commit (nine columns)" "$(yn [ "$(head -n 1 "$TXT")" = "$TXT_HEADER" ])"
    tail -n +2 "$TXT" | cut -f1-5 >"$B/txt.rows"
    nrow_same=$(paste -d'\n' "$B/keep.rows" "$B/txt.rows" | awk 'NR % 2 == 1 { a = $0; next } a == $0 { n++ } END { print n + 0 }')
    echo "  rows: the keep $(count_lines "$B/keep.rows"), the .txt $(count_lines "$B/txt.rows"); rows whose name, bytes and hashes are the keep's, compared row by row: $nrow_same"
    rows_same() { [ "$(count_lines "$B/keep.rows")" = "$(count_lines "$B/txt.rows")" ] && [ "$nrow_same" = "$(count_lines "$B/keep.rows")" ] && [ "$nrow_same" = "$NPAIRS" ]; }
    check "every .txt row is one kept pair's name, byte counts and sha256s, in name order, one row per pair" "$(yn rows_same)"
    bad_rows=$(tail -n +2 "$TXT" | awk -F'\t' 'NF != 9 || $6 !~ /^(ok|fail|error)$/ || $7 !~ /^(ok|fail|error)$/ || $8 !~ /^(none|refused|count|error)$/ || $9 !~ /^(none|refused|count|error)$/' | wc -l)
    check "every row has nine columns, lo_in and lo each ok, fail or error, and each class none, refused, count or error ($bad_rows rows otherwise)" "$(yn [ "$bad_rows" = 0 ])"
    bad_fit=$(tail -n +2 "$TXT" | awk -F'\t' '{ print $6 ":" $8; print $7 ":" $9 }' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -cvxE 'ok:none|fail:refused|fail:count|error:error')
    check "every side's class fits its verdict ($bad_fit sides otherwise)" "$(yn [ "$bad_fit" = 0 ])"
    stdout_rows() { [ "$(awk -F'\t' 'NF == 3' "$B/oc.stdout")" = "$(tail -n +2 "$TXT" | cut -f1,6,7)" ]; }
    check "the script's per-pair stdout lines are the .txt's test, lo_in and lo columns" "$(yn stdout_rows)"
    echo "command: python3 <work>/wb.py over each kept input: its xl/workbook.xml entry, its sheet elements by local name (expat, no pattern) and of them those with a prefix"
    cat >"$B/wb.py" <<'PY'
    import sys, zipfile
    from xml.parsers import expat
    for path in sys.argv[1:]:
        name = path.rsplit("/", 1)[1][: -len(".in.xlsx")]
        try:
            z = zipfile.ZipFile(path)
        except zipfile.BadZipFile:
            print("%s\tunreadable\t-\t-" % name)
            continue
        if "xl/workbook.xml" not in z.namelist():
            print("%s\tno\t-\t-" % name)
            continue
        found = {"all": 0, "prefixed": 0}
    
        def start(tag, attrs):
            prefix, _, local = tag.rpartition(":")
            if local == "sheet":
                found["all"] += 1
                found["prefixed"] += 1 if prefix else 0
        p = expat.ParserCreate()
        p.StartElementHandler = start
        try:
            p.Parse(z.read("xl/workbook.xml"), True)
        except expat.ExpatError:
            print("%s\tyes\tunparsed\t-" % name)
            continue
        print("%s\tyes\t%d\t%d" % (name, found["all"], found["prefixed"]))
    PY
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/wb.py"
    python3 "$B/wb.py" $(sed "s#^#$KEEP/#; s#\$#.in.xlsx#" "$B/pair.names") | LC_ALL=C sort >"$B/wb.all"
    echo "  kept inputs by workbook entry and sheet elements (entry, all, prefixed: pairs):"
    cut -f2- "$B/wb.all" | sort | uniq -c | sed 's/^/    /'
    echo "  the .md checked against the .txt and the kept inputs, with the heading specs/0015 P2 verification ruling 1 gives: <work>/mdcheck.py, below"
    cat >"$B/mdcheck.py" <<'PY'
    import sys
    txt, md, wb = sys.argv[1:4]
    rows = [l.split("\t") for l in open(txt).read().split("\n")[1:] if l]
    sheets = {l.split("\t")[0]: l.split("\t")[2] for l in open(wb).read().split("\n") if l}
    text = open(md).read().split("\n")
    REFUSED = ("Inputs refused by LibreOffice (allowed: a fixture LibreOffice cannot load: zip-level,"
               " or a package with no relationships part or an empty content-types root)")
    
    
    def section(title):
        out, on = [], False
        for line in text:
            if line == "## " + title:
                on = True
                continue
            if on and line.startswith("## "):
                break
            if on and line:
                out.append(line)
        return out
    
    
    def listed(names):
        return ["- `%s`" % n for n in names] if names else ["None."]
    
    
    def count(col, v):
        return sum(1 for r in rows if r[col] == v)
    
    
    totals = [len(rows)] + [count(5, v) for v in ("ok", "fail", "error")] + [count(6, v) for v in ("ok", "fail", "error")]
    classes = ["| %s | " % side + " | ".join(str(count(col, c)) for c in ("none", "refused", "count", "error")) + " |"
               for side, col in (("reason_in", 7), ("reason_out", 8))]
    tot = section("Totals")
    checks = [
        ("Totals", tot[2:3] == ["| " + " | ".join(str(t) for t in totals) + " |"] and tot[5:] == classes),
        ("the refused-inputs heading reads as ruled, once", text.count("## " + REFUSED) == 1),
        ("Inputs refused by LibreOffice", section(REFUSED) == listed([r[0] for r in rows if r[7] == "refused"])),
        ("the sheet count did not apply", section("Inputs the sheet count did not apply to (allowed: a workbook fixture with no sheet element)") == listed([r[0] for r in rows if r[7] == "count" and sheets.get(r[0]) == "0"])),
        ("counts differ", section("Inputs whose sheet and table counts differ (a finding)") == listed([r[0] for r in rows if r[7] == "count" and sheets.get(r[0]) != "0"])),
        ("Outputs refused on an accepted input", section("Outputs refused on an input LibreOffice accepted (a finding)") == listed([r[0] for r in rows if r[6] == "fail" and r[5] == "ok"])),
        ("Checks that did not run", section("Checks that did not run (error)") == listed([r[0] for r in rows if "error" in (r[5], r[6])])),
        ("Pairs", section("Pairs")[2:] == ["| `%s` | %s | %s | %s | %s | %s | %s | %s | %s |" % tuple(r) for r in rows]),
        ("the Pairs line", ("- Pairs: %d" % len(rows)) in text),
    ]
    for name, ok in checks:
        print("%s: %s" % (name, "yes" if ok else "no"))
    print("totals: pairs %d; lo_in ok %d fail %d error %d; lo ok %d fail %d error %d" % tuple(totals))
    PY
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/mdcheck.py"
